{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/239065-ic-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign","id":239065,"title":"[IC] [Exalted] The Whitestone Island Campaign","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play","Play by Post"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-24T06:51:44-07:00","id":239065,"title":"[IC] [Exalted] The Whitestone Island Campaign","content":"<b>Calm Sea Village, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour after Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> It was a beautiful morning, and it was looking like it was going to be a beautiful day. There had been a light rain in the hours before dawn, and the morning sun glistened in golden drops on the huge leaves of the banana orchards. Roosters were crowing and strutting their wawy about on the thatched rooftops of Calm Sea Village, and people were waking up and going about their morning routines. The fishermen had all woken up hours ago, and the sails of their double-canoes were visible as white triangles out on the sapphire horizon.<br /> <br /> The Season of Fire was a relaxed time on Whitestone Island. It was a time of harvesting, as elsewhere in Creation, a time when the growth brought about by the rains of the Season of Water and the calm weather of the Season of Earth bore fruit. Women with knives would be out soon, cutting down bunches of bananas for frying or baking into chips for later in the year. Children would be climbing trees and jumping up and down on branches to make breadnuts fall into nets held by their elders below, and yelling at monkeys to scare them away from avocados and papayas. Beach farmers would be reeling in mats overgrown with seaweed for the harvest, or rowing out in canoes to pull up lines hung from wooden bouys earlier in the year to harvest the shelfish that had grown on them for great stews and soups. By the time the heat of the afternoon rose up and tamped down the village's enthusiasm for work, the beaches south of the village would be full of tired people and excited children playing in the surf, or fishing, or wading with spears in search of dinner. The evening would be warm and dark and full of singing and dancing and drinking.<br /> <br /> Of course, Huelo, who had just been woken by a particularly enthusiastic rooster right outside his window after staying up far too late breaking up a dispute between two drunken fishermen over a minor collision, was having trouble enjoying the season just at the moment.<br /> <br /> <b>In The Mountains Northeast of Thousand Lilies Village, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, At Sunrise</b><br /> <br /> It was a beautiful morning, and it looked like it was going to be a beautiful day. The sun was just cresting over the Eastern horizon, illuminating several puffy white clouds in fantastic shades of pink and orange against the darkness of the vertical cliff face rising up ahead. It had rained an hour or so before, and the jungle was full of glints of morning light caught in droplets of water. The jungle floor was starting to fill with fog, and soon that fog would rise up the mountainside in great steaming clouds full of sneaky little rainbows before dissipating in the sun.<br /> <br /> Wahine and Seskan had spent the last hour marching through a thick jungle full of unpleasantly sturdy plants just the right height to smack you in sensitive bits of your anatomy when you walked into them in the dark. It had been drizzling lightly when they left Thousand Lilies Village, and an hour stomping through the jungle carrying large backpacks full of wood and laquer had left them sopping wet and covered in mosquito bites. Even Cloudhopper Haku, who had made this trek a thousand times and was trying to impress an attractive woman with his ruggedness and stoic mastery of the jungle, had seemed affected by something of a sour mood.<br /> <br /> It was gone now, though. He sat on a high bluff overlooking the sunrise and the river and more jungle far below, fastening straps and double-checking to make sure that Seskan had unfolded and properly donned his glider. Wahine had seen Haku grinning like this a few times before and even at a similar angle, for she was belted tightly to him and facing forward so that she had to turn her head to look backwards.<br /> <br /> Finally, the warrior seemed satisfied that Seskan at least could not blame Alial Darumi's old glider for it if he got himself killed, and he stood back with a grin.<br /> <br /> &quot;Alright, we're all strapped in, the sun is up, and the warm air is starting to rise. You two ready to jump off this cliff?&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>On the Deck of the Guild Ship <i>Blue Lily</i>, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour after Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> It was a beautiful morning. A good stiff breeze from the southeast filled the sails, the light clouds before sunrise had cleared enough for a good view of the stars, and the crew seemed in high spirits after last night's music and singing and dancing on the deck. Even Menreiki, who had been belowdecks battling seasickness, finally seemed to have gotten his sea legs and had come topside to sign and dance and entertain the crew.<br /> <br /> Captain Phi Ho stood at the helm, the warm breeze ruffling his whiskers. He growled in pleasure. Sailing was his joy, but sailing into uncharted waters...that was his true passion. The cabin boy, a nephew he had agreed to train in his trade, was taking notes. The boy had a good head on his shoulders, he'd been recording Phi Ho's observations of the stars. Menreiki's strange protege claimed there was an island out here somewhere, an island she had seen in her dreams, and Captain Phi Ho was determined to be the first to put it on a map. Flying Tiger Island, he'd call it. Or perhaps Tiger's Landing...<br /> <br /> Ah, there she was now. The Maiden, as the crew and her fans called her, climbed her way up from belowdecks, and the breeze tousled her raven hair. Phi Ho smiled. She rose early every morning, sometimes before dawn. Curling Willow, who bunked in the cabin next door and had very good ears, claimed that she suffered from nightmares, for he occasionally heard her wake with a startled noise and heard the sleep-addled Menreiki thump across the passenger cabin to comfort her. Upon learning of this Captain Phi Ho, gentleman that he was, had ordered the cook to have an early breakfast prepared every morning just in case the Maiden wanted one. He gave the cabin boy a brief nod and a shove, and the boy darted off to gather up the boiled egg and the cheese and tray of dried fruit and bowl of sweet porridge that had been readied against this eventuality about an hour before.<br /> <br /> Menreiki, artist that he was, always slept in until at least eleven.<br /> <br /> &quot;Good morning, Milady,&quot; the Captain purred, and his deep voice rumbled across the deck. &quot;I hope you slept well?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>OOC: There will be an opening post for Pakari and the Bearer of Bones in the next day or two. Still waiting on a character sheet for Lyndon, but I'ma start you two off without him.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T23:17:36-07:00","id":242857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/239065-ic-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign#post239065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>In The Mountains Northeast of Thousand Lilies Village, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, At Sunrise</b></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wahine enjoyed the early morning hours when she could listen to the world wake up. The sounds of the rivers, the ocean, the wind, and the earth where like listening to creation breathe. As the sky began to lighten, the empty forests would fill with the sounds of songbirds and other animals. She liked the chorus of birds most of all. Not that she could hear much today over the wracket of pack laden men lumbering through the jungle.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">She wasn\u2019t at all impressed by Haku\u2019s display of \u201cruggedness\u201d. She spent at least as much time in the jungle as he did and often chose camping over village lodging.</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> It would take a lot more than carrying a heavy pack on a short hike to impress her. Her spirits where pretty high in spite of the recent rainfall and proliferation of mosquitoes. She smirked in the darkness whenever she heard sounds of frustration or the regretful groans of a large man walking into something unfortunate. The morning was proving entertaining so far.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A stubby red tail fluttered in front of her, hopping from perch to perch. \u201cOoo! Ouch! OOOoooowww!\u201d her ash colored bird sang aloud as the group pushed their way through the jungle. Many years and many islands ago she\u2019d aquired the odd colored</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> creature and he\u2019d been her \u2018little shadow\u2019 ever since. There was no telling where he'd originally come from or how many hands he\u2019d passed through before winding up in her remote corner of the west. His last owner thought him a stubborn, ill-tempered creature. When the bird began to take a shine to Wahine, the man was more than glad to get rid of him. He was a clever devil and a bit of a clown at times but for her he was always gentle and affectionate. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Assembling the other man\u2019s beat up glider seemed an incredibly cumbersome task. <i>There\u2019s got to be a better way to do this...</i>her mind toyed with a few ideas while she watched Haku help the other man. She wasn\u2019t sure if she\u2019d seen the man before. Addmittedly she didn\u2019t socialize much with many of villagers. Wahine was not a small woman but belted to Haku\u2019s massive bulk she sure felt small. Hell, even a young ox would probably feel smaller and slight strapped to his broad chest. That stupid grin of his was infectious. He may be an oaf but at least he was a chearful oaf. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Her bird toddled around on the ground, hopping up and down excitedly. \u201cJump! Jump! Jump!\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wahine pointed forward towards the open sky.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","user":"Foxsimile","date":". 08-28-2014, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T05:16:00-07:00","id":243014,"title":"","content":"<b>In the Jungle About One Day's Hike from Dreaming River Village, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Shortly After Sunrise</b><br /> <br /> It was a beautiful morning, and it was looking like it was going to turn into a beautiful day.<br /> <br /> Yesterday had been kind of scary, Master Hasya had stood in front of a huge and angry looking stone face jutting out of the mountainside and looked really worried and talked about the wards falling apart after the big storm last week, and needing to fix something up as soon as possible, because apparently the mouth of the huge angry looking stone face led into an ancient tomb guarded by a fearsome demon. The New Moon was only six days away, and if the wards that had gotten damaged during the storm weren't back up by then...well, Pakari didn't actually know, because master Hasya had just trailed off when he said it, but it probably wasn't anything good.<br /> <br /> So yesterday had been kind of worrisome, but today was looking lovely! There had been a pleasant rain a few hours ago, and Pakari had watched some tree spirits come out and dance in the branches, and he had listened to the gentle music of the tapping of drops on leaves and the whispered song of branches in the breeze, and as he walked the rain had faded and the sun had started to come out. The tree spirits, little green and brown creatures the size of a child with trailing leaves and brightly colored flowers for hair and long slender fingers and toes, stopped their dance and turned to face the sun and going silent for a while as it broke the horizon. Then they clambered off into the higher canopy of the jungle and he lost sight of them for a while.<br /> <br /> The air smelled good, the spirits seemed happy, and he was going home. Not to stay long, to be sure, Master Hasya had been very clear on that point. But gathering up some rope and some candles and a few gourds full of pig's blood and some white chalk and several kinds of incense that Master Hasya had written down so he didn't forget them wouldn't take too long, and even the wooden wind chimes shouldn't be too hard, he knew there were some at the temple already.<br /> <br /> ...by the gods, the air smelled good. In fact, it smelled faintly of well-cooked pork and woodsmoke. Up ahead, Pakara saw the dim flicker of a campfire. He also noticed several forest spirits sitting on the branches glaring down at the clearing in which the campfire was located, whispering occasionally to each other in angry voices.<br /> <br /> As he approached, there was a loud crack sound as a tree limb loosened by the storm finally fell, collapsing a lean-to made out of palm leaves onto its suddenly awake inhabitant.<br /> <br /> Sopping wet, running low on meat from the last small wild pig she's caught, troubles by unpleasant dreams, and now thrashing inside the ruins of her water-drenched tent after having been smacked in the lower back by a sizeable tree branch, the Bearer of Bones' morning was looking to be anything but beautiful.<br /> <br /> <b>In The Mountains Northeast of Thousand Lilies Village, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, At Sunrise</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Ha ha!&quot; Haku's voice rumbled, and vibrated Wahine's body as he chuckled. It felt a little bit like lying on the ground on the warm southern beaches when the volcano on Sunset Island shook the earth. &quot;Looks like your friend here is looking forward to flying with us! Seskan, I know you've taken a few practice runs with Darumi, but remember you're going to be lighter without him, so you're going to turn faster and it'll be easier to spin yourself and lose your bearings. If you're going to crash, you're going to do it taking off now or landing at the end. Slow, gentle movements, even at the beginning when you're falling. I'm going to go ahead of you and aim for the warm rising air. Follow our path. If you aim it wrong and miss the rising air, aim for the bushes on the other side of the river. Don't try any fancy tricks today, and don't try to copy me if I do any-just basic flying. I don't want to have to explain to Darumi why his glider's broken!&quot;<br /> <br /> With that, he turned and walked away from the edge of the bluff to get some run-up distance, the long wings of his glider bobbing gently as he moved.<br /> <br /> &quot;Here...we...go!&quot;<br /> <br /> Twelve huge bouncing steps and a leap and a brief moment of purely instinctual terror later, Wahine was soaring through the air, gliding down over the river, over the forest on the other side, and into the swell of warm air rising up the side of the cliff. Haku jostled her slightly as he tilted his weight and pulled some control straps to bring them into a slow circling climb. With a flutter of grey-white feathers, her bird enthusiastically flashed ahead of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 08-28-2014, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T09:52:11-07:00","id":243217,"title":"","content":"Pakari gave a start when he heard the crack and watched as the limb fell onto a shelter below. Based on the muffled, angry-sounding racket coming from within, there was definitely someone in there. When his muscles caught up to his mind, Pakari pushed forward through the undergrowth, grabbed and lifted the fallen branch with both hands, and heaved it to one side.<br /> <br /> Underneath, still partially buried in leaves, was a large woman, older than Pakari but not yet an elder. She looked upset, probably because a large tree branch had disrupted her sleep and nearly crushed her. She had Whispering Valley tribe tattoos, but as far as Pakari could tell she looked like a coastal tribeswoman. Stranger still, she seemed to be wearing an old Temple Guardian cloak, but Pakari thought he knew all the Guadians, and he was sure he hadn't met this one before.<br /> <br /> Lying on the ground by her side was a worn-looking cloth bundle. Pakari squinted at it and realized it was actually a child in swaddling cloth - Yet more strangeness, since Guardians were not supposed to have children. Then he noticed the state of the &quot;child's&quot; hair and dessicated face, and his confusion grew. It wasn't a child - it was the mummified corpse of a child!<br /> <br /> Finally, things clicked together in Pakari's head. This must be the Bearer of the Bones - Pakari had seen her at a distance a few times, but never spoken to her. Hasya had told him that she used to be a Guardian, that she carried the wrapped body of a child everywhere as an act of penance for the child's death, and that she was to be pitied. She did not ask for or accept hospitality as most people would. That was the beginning and end of everything Pakari knew about her.<br /> <br /> Pakari was not sure what to do. How does one address a pariah? After a moment's hesitation, he decided to err on the side of compassion and sat down on his haunches by her side. &quot;Are you alright... Ma'am?&quot; he asked, scanning her for signs of injury. She was probably fine, but it was better to check - and perhaps a little kindness would make her rude awakening sting a little less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 08-28-2014, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T09:29:20-07:00","id":244049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/239065-ic-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign#post239065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>On the Deck of the Guild Ship <i>Blue Lily</i>, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour after Sunrise:</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The Maiden opened her eyes, and her face covered in sweats. The nightmare that that has plagued her for the past few month has started to occurred more and more frequently, &quot;Why must I be tortured like this, have I done something wrong in my past life ?&quot;. It's only then that her master's snore broke the Maiden out of her trance.<br /> <br /> Letting out a heavy sigh, the Maiden leave her bed and started to change her attire. The fresh smell of the ocean air at least helped to make her feel a little more relax as she leave the cabin, ah yes, she can see captain Phi H\u1ed5 behind the ship wheel, and all the crewman seem to in a bright mood too. The Maiden smiled lightly as she remembered how joyful the last night performance was, even her master decided to join in for a last minute duet.<br /> <br /> A softly-spoken and yet husky voice politely offered the Maiden a good morning greeting, &quot;Thank you for taking care of me for these last few weeks.&quot;, the Maiden respectfully bowed to return the captain's kindness.<br /> <br /> &quot;Aayeee, have we reached the Middle-of-Nowhere Island yet ?&quot;, a half-asleep figure started to emerge from below the deck, &quot;My back gonna turn to dust if I have to sleep in these wretched bed one more night&quot;, the Maiden and the Captain's miens began to go from calm to annoyed at the rabbit-ear man who was stretching his arms behind his back while letting out a big yawn.<br /> <br /> Captain Phi H\u1ed5 quickly resumed his cool and collected demeanor to answer Menreiki's question, &quot;I'm sure you must be so uncomfortable that you always keep sleeping until the Daystar hit its peak. But don't worry, look to the front.&quot;<br /> <br /> The island in the girl dream was starting to appear before their eyes. A strange sense dread overpower the Maiden for just a moment, her master on the other hand seem to snap-out of his drowsy state immediately and was seem to fill with eagerness and excitement. <div align=\"center\"><b>&quot;Come back....to Sunset Island&quot;</b></div> <br /> The black-haired girl frowned as a half-remembered voice echoed in her head. But there can't be no turning back now, the Maiden wanted to know for sure what is happening to her and to make sure that she will regain her lost memories. The towering silhouette of the island began to get bigger, she can already saw the ivory sand decorated the shore like a necklace of pure white jade. <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i1196.photobucket.com/albums/aa418/crimsonorigami/imagejpg1-9.jpg~original\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 08-29-2014, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T12:26:35-07:00","id":245559,"title":"","content":"Seskan hated that day.<br /> <br /> It all was Ailal's fault. He was the one to mention that stupid &quot;name ritual&quot; at the first place. Sure, he knew that his friend only meant well by suggesting him to pass the ritual- after all, all of those who lived on the island did so- so he agreed. How in the name of all of the demons in the Demon City he should have known that Ailal would decide that he should go to the nearest ritual, getting the agreement of both the Chief and the High Priestess behind his back (he wanted to surprise him and thought that it would make him happy) and finding some old friend to help him teach Seskan to use the kite. When he mentioned that he didn't had a glider, Ailal suggested to give him his old one- but that was his limit. That was the time he gave up, and has started to think seriously that he may have survived drowning in the city only to be eaten by a giant eel.<br /> <br /> The walk in the forest itself wasn't that bad- he may have even enjoyed it if he wouldn't have thought constantly about the reason he went to that &quot;trip&quot;. Sure, he was bitten by insects and was scratched by thorns, but he saw many new and exciting things- plants which were rare in his island were common in here, and all kinds of new animals surrounded him. The singing of the exotic birds fascinated him, and he constantly thought which kinds of ingredients he could gather for his spells and potions. Yet, more interesting than the jungle were his escorts.<br /> <br /> It was obvious what the man (Haku, he believed) tried to achieve- after all, he paid less attention to the one he was meant to teach and more for the other escort, the woman (which he didn't got her name). The woman was truly interesting- after all, Ailal has warned him that she can't speak and that he should respect her silence. That, of course, made Seskan a lot more curious, for it meant that perhaps there is some secret hidden in that woman- but it wasn't the time to search for secrets. It was the time to find a way to survive his trial.<br /> <br /> When he got to they got to the cliff, the only thing he could think about was if he could find a way out of that. He thought about using his skills in order to enchant the glider somehow, but he wasn't sure that no one would notice and that it won't be considered as cheating. He thought that maybe he could find some good reason to try and postpone his participation, like creating some potion that would make him sick (yes, he was desperate enough to think about poisoning himself), yet he understood that it was only a temporary solution, for if he wished to become a true part of the society in the island he had to do the ritual. Plus, because of Ailal, the attention of the High Priestess was focused on him, and if he'll withdraw she would remember it- and his chances at becoming one of the Temple Guardians would vanish like mist in the sun.<br /> <br /> And so, he stood on the edge of the cliff, doing his best in order to not look down. Suddenly, the talking bird of the woman has started to scream, calling &quot;Jump!&quot; again and again. Seskan had to use all of his self control in order not to choke the damn bird, while fantasizing about summoning a demon and ordering it to eat the damn thing. Finally, he took a deep breath, closed his eyes, touched the charm his mentor has given him one last time and prayed for what ever power that saved him from the storm to protect him from a far more ridiculous death. Then, he was ready.<br /> <br /> He looked directly at the far, blue skies, and jumped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T08:58:21-07:00","id":246174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Calm Sea Village, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour after Sunrise:</b><br /> Of course, Huelo, who had just been woken by a particularly enthusiastic rooster right outside his window after staying up far too late breaking up a dispute between two drunken fishermen over a minor collision, was having trouble enjoying the season just at the moment. </div> </div> </div>&quot;...one of these mornings I am going to wake up to a nice quite morning, and fresh fried chicken.&quot; The man who was trying to bring law and order to the island was dealing with the head-aches of bringing law and order. Things like dealing with drunk fishermen who couldn't figure out how right of way when sober, reaching out to him in to deal with it when both were so drunk that seeing strait was a long forgotten memory was both an insult and a compliment. It was a compliment in that they actually understood how having law enforcement on the island works, which given their condition that level of clear thinking was impressive.<br /> <br /> It was insulting to think that this was the only time that the only time they would turn to him was in matters like that. It was a start though perhaps that one day they will open up more and more to law and the safety it brings. Taking his trunchon and sword down from the wall by his mat he removes the sheets and walks over to the basin and washes his face. He tries to remember if there is anyone locked up below in the jail.<br /> <br /> After getting ready for his day the man walks down into the jail to start his day with a hot beverage and some local fruit. Some things should be in season by now. Walking down into the Jail he sits in his official chair, behind his official desk. The desk was drift wood from a shipwreck that he had just finished nailing together recently. The chair was a likewise made from salvage. One day he hoped to get proper desks and chairs but this was not that day, or month, maybe not year.<br /> <br /> With that done he looks to the jail cells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T12:06:45-07:00","id":246292,"title":"","content":"&quot;Fine,&quot; said the bonebearer, in a tone of voice one should reserve for enemies, as she tore off what leaves still covered her and her meagre belongings. That done, and her sword-clubs and shield accounted for, she settled into a more comfortable, seated position.<br /> &quot;No reason for you to be here. Are you lost?&quot;<br /> As she quickly scanned her charge (dead, sleeping) and fire (choked by a wet branch) and breakfast (sooty), fierce pale eyes could be glimpsed in the shadow of her matted hair.<br /> &quot;Help yourself,&quot; and here she cocked her head towards of the still-edible pork in the ashes, &quot;better a child eats than I.&quot;<br /> <br /> It was only now that she actually <i>looked</i> at Pakari, and the size of him seemed to startle her. When next she spoke, her tone was somewhat less grim.<br /> &quot;Better a young man eats than I,&quot; she corrected herself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 09-01-2014, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T10:52:32-07:00","id":246949,"title":"","content":"Pakari stood up and stepped back as the Bearer collected herself. &quot;I'm not lost, I'm traveling,&quot; he said, noting her armaments as she gathered them up - did she expect to be attacked, or was she looking for a fight? &quot;Going to Dreaming River Village. For supplies.&quot; ...and also probably to waste a few hours telling Aunt Aroha and others everything he'd been up to since his last visit, but Pakari didn't think the Bearer would be interested in that part. He wanted to ask what she was doing out here herself, but he suppressed the reflexive return question. She might be out here simply because she would not be welcome in any of the villages, or because it was part of her penance, or to commune with the spirits. Whatever it was, what she was doing wasn't really any of his business.<br /> <br /> He looked at the campfire. A chunk of meat had dropped into the coals, but it was probably still good. He'd been brought up not to refuse hospitality, or to waste food, and he was kind of hungry - he'd set out before dawn and hadn't stopped to eat, figuring that Aroha would insist on cooking (way too much food) for him when he arrived. Pakari looked back to the bearer, bowed his head, and said &quot;Thank you,&quot; before grabbing a palm leaf from the ground. He brushed it off and used the damp leaf to grab the warm pork out of the fire circle, dusting off some of the ash with his fingers before taking a bite. It was a little burnt, but Pakari didn't much care - roast pork was always good to start the morning with.<br /> <br /> He tore the meat hunk in half and proffered the part he hadn't bitten to the Bearer. &quot;You sure you don't want any? It's not bad.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 09-02-2014, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T17:46:15-07:00","id":251167,"title":"","content":"<b>In the Mountains Northeast of Thousand Lilies Village, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, At Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Seskan, I made a prayer roll for you (Two successes) and a Dex+Ride roll to get the glider in the air (One Success). You were doing it under perfect conditions with no penalties, and I gave you a situational bonus of two dice to take off due to following Haku's example. Flying your beginner's glider reasonably easy, so I won't require additional piloting rolls for basic travel. If you attempt any aerobatic maneuvers, or if you attempt a controlled rise or descent, or if you encounter any weather or when it comes time for you to land, I'll have you make additional rolls.</i><br /> <br /> Seskan experienced a lurch and a rising of his stomach into his throat before the adrenaline kicked in and he found himself filled with excitement. His practice with Alial came back to his hands without conscious thought, and he tilted his weight and pulled the straps to steer his glider without thought. He descended rapidly toward the river, and for a brief moment he worried he might crash, but then he pulled up slightly and his wings of laquer and sailcloth caught the rising breeze, and he soared over the treetops in a wide circle as he'd practiced when strapped to Alial and as Haku had instructed.<br /> <br /> <b>High Above Whitestone Island, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, About Half An Hour Later:</b><br /> <br /> Both gliders had ridden the warm thermals up the side of the mountain and into the silent air high above the birds that flitted and fluttered over the forest far below. Seskan and Wahine could see the buildings of Thousand Lilies village studding the green hills above Green Lake like children's toys. The sun glinted off the lake, and off the sea which was now visible extending out to the horizon beyond the shores of the island. The sun shone low in the eastern skies, which were clear and bright and blue. As Seskan followed Haku and Wahine as they soared over the mountains separating the lands of the Green Flower and Sunset tribes, they could see the eastern horizon shining blue past the lush green of Whitestone Island, and a faint triangular shadow to the distant east which the gliders all used to orient themselves if they found their directions getting mixed up.<br /> <br /> Sunset Island rose on the southern horizon, and a gentle column of smoke rose high into the air like a smear of diluted ink, growing fainter and fainter and wider and wider as it climbed. The only sounds were the creak of laminated wood and the flutter of the cloth that made up the wings and the gentle rustling of the breeze.<br /> <br /> &quot;We're heading south!&quot; Haku yelled to Seskan. &quot;We'll make a circuit on the southern shores, and ride the wind up the Whispering Valley Mountains to give us enough height to get home!&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Seskan and Wahine, please give me a Perception+Awareness roll on the next posts. Also, Seskan, feel free to converse with Haku, you're within shouting distance. Wahine, sorry to sort of strap you in for the ride. I know you can't really shout to communicate, but feel free to have your trained bird get you in on the interaction if you like.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Calm Sea Village, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour after Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> The jail cells (constructed at his instructions from the materials available, which meant the walls were built in a heavier log-cabin style than the other buildings of the village, and the bars were cut saplings and the doors were held shut by means of a heavy wooden beam which could not be reached from inside the cells) were mostly empty, save only for Faruma Black Eyes, who had two weeks ago gotten drunk and tried to burn down his ex-lover's hut. Faruma was still asleep on his cot in the corner. His family had requested that a priest from outside the village be sent to decide upon the appropriate punishment for his crime, as his lover was the nephew of the priest who ran the local temple, and it was clear that impartiality was difficult to establish in his case. Normally the priest would just render a verdict after hearing both sides of the story and the people of the village would see it carried out, but Faruma's grandfather was a cousin to Fokisi's grandmother, and therefore had ties with the nobility back in Two Rivers village where the tribal Chieftain dwelled, and so it was important that justice was seen to be carried out fairly. Of course, the victim's family claimed that the priest being sent would obviously favor Faruma because of his family's clout, so the Black Eye clan had arranged for a priestess stationed in the Dreaming River tribe who cared not one with for local politics to be sent out to arbitrate the case...which all meant that Faruma would have a few more weeks to wait in the cells while she made her way here.<br /> <br /> He was well-behaved and had sworn off drink several times a day for the past few days.<br /> <br /> As Huelo did his daily inspection and munched his breakfast, the door opened, letting in a gentle breeze and the pleasant smells of the village outside.<br /> <br /> &quot;Good morning!&quot; Nemoai declared in a cheerful voice. He carried a heavy basket. &quot;Got a big pile of yams here, from Leilo Sweet-Tide, thanks for sorting out her husband's stupid fight last night. She says to tell you she'll make sure he doesn't take any more drink with him when he ships out in the morning, and that she's sending another basket to the Breaking Wave's wife to apologize for her husband running into their boat.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>On the Deck of the Guild Ship Blue Lily, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour after Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Ahoy! Land!&quot; shouted someone from the crow's nest.<br /> <br /> &quot;We see it already!&quot; Phi Ho shouted back. &quot;And wake up, up there! All hands on deck! We've spotted land!&quot;<br /> <br /> Suddenly the ship was bustling with life. Sailors clambered up and down the rigging, tightening and loosening sails to adjust the ship's course. In the midst of the frenetic activity, the ship came up with a tray with a boiled egg and some sliced cheese, as well as a selection of dried fruit, for Menreiki and the Maiden. He promised to return shortly with some breakfast wine, and scurried off belowdecks.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ahoy! Another island!&quot; came the call from the crow's nest. &quot;Off the port bow!&quot;<br /> <br /> Ahead, a conical island rose slowly from the place where sea met sky, a gentle column of smoke rising from its volcanic peak. Slightly more distant, another, larger island was coming into view, its rolling green mountains filling up much of the horizon.<br /> <br /> The Maiden had a sudden memory of bare toes and hot sand, of laughter...she didn't know whose laughter.<br /> <br /> &quot;With the wind as it is, we should arrive in about half an hour,&quot; Phi Ho declared to Menreiki. &quot;Though it may take longer to find a safe harbor to weigh anchor. The weather's fine today, but this far West squalls can come up out of nowhere...I don't suppose your companion remembers the shape of the place, or could point us to a nice sheltered bay or inlet?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 09-08-2014, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T20:17:07-07:00","id":251888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Calm Sea Village, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour after Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> The jail cells (constructed at his instructions from the materials available, which meant the walls were built in a heavier log-cabin style than the other buildings of the village, and the bars were cut saplings and the doors were held shut by means of a heavy wooden beam which could not be reached from inside the cells) were mostly empty, save only for Faruma Black Eyes, who had two weeks ago gotten drunk and tried to burn down his ex-lover's hut. Faruma was still asleep on his cot in the corner. His family had requested that a priest from outside the village be sent to decide upon the appropriate punishment for his crime, as his lover was the nephew of the priest who ran the local temple, and it was clear that impartiality was difficult to establish in his case. Normally the priest would just render a verdict after hearing both sides of the story and the people of the village would see it carried out, but Faruma's grandfather was a cousin to Fokisi's grandmother, and therefore had ties with the nobility back in Two Rivers village where the tribal Chieftain dwelled, and so it was important that justice was seen to be carried out fairly. Of course, the victim's family claimed that the priest being sent would obviously favor Faruma because of his family's clout, so the Black Eye clan had arranged for a priestess stationed in the Dreaming River tribe who cared not one with for local politics to be sent out to arbitrate the case...which all meant that Faruma would have a few more weeks to wait in the cells while she made her way here.<br /> <br /> He was well-behaved and had sworn off drink several times a day for the past few days.<br /> <br /> As Huelo did his daily inspection and munched his breakfast, the door opened, letting in a gentle breeze and the pleasant smells of the village outside.<br /> <br /> &quot;Good morning!&quot; Nemoai declared in a cheerful voice. He carried a heavy basket. &quot;Got a big pile of yams here, from Leilo Sweet-Tide, thanks for sorting out her husband's stupid fight last night. She says to tell you she'll make sure he doesn't take any more drink with him when he ships out in the morning, and that she's sending another basket to the Breaking Wave's wife to apologize for her husband running into their boat.&quot; </div> </div> </div>&quot;I swear some men have wives just to keep them from getting killed.&quot; He smiles looking at his 'deputy'. &quot;Good work Nemoai.&quot; I set the basket aside. I get some simple food for the man in the jail cell and put the cold food and a cup of water down for our prisoner. This is the longest we have had someone stay here. My past few have just been drunk tank arrests and I've just held them till they could sleep it off. This one was different. I wanted him to have a fair hearing, and I wanted justice, fair and equitable. I hoped he got it. &quot;Eat up, it's a new day, and a new chance.&quot; I look at him sternly. I had hopes for him. There was a chance he could repent, though it seems the demon of drink is getting to be a bigger problem here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T01:16:55-07:00","id":252084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/239065-ic-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign?p=251167#post251167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>In the Mountains Northeast of Thousand Lilies Village, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, At Sunrise:</b><br /> <b>High Above Whitestone Island, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, About Half An Hour Later:</b><br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Seskan and Wahine, please give me a Perception+Awareness roll on the next posts.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Jumping from the cliff face was always exhilarating. Could she speak, Wahine would have let out an excited shout as the glider lurched downward and then suddenly upward as air filled the lacquer braced sail cloth. Instead, her wild smile and silent laughter spoke for her. </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Joy shone from her face like a beacon as she marveled at the morning before them and took in the scenery with wide eyed amazement. From their lofty height she could see far beyond the swath of land she knew intimately and could appreciate the size of the island and the vastness of the sea beyond. As familiar landforms and landmarks passed beneath them, she kept a weather eye out for signs of her rare few friends and familiar acquaintances. She whistled loudly, listening for a reply from the vague shapes or other unseen persons who knew her calls. Her bird drifted amongst the gliders in languid patterns, lending his own voice to Wahine\u2019s calls. Soon they rose too high for anyone below to hear and she became absorbed with the grander view. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Nothing could dampen her spirits. She made a face at the other glider as Haku circled around in an updraft. As they settled in for the longer flight, she was even feeling unusually tolerant of Haku's often affectionate company. If his attention became too amorous for her liking, she was more than flexible enough to jab him in the sides like a stubborn mount. A swift kick with her heels would set him straight. But so far she was enjoying the attention. Her bird started to sing songs to entertain himself as they followed the updrafts and currents. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">\u201cLady, Lady give me your answer true</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Will you let me fly along with you?</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">When you and I go cruisin\u2019</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">You\u2019ll thank me for choosin\u2019</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">You to come and have some fun</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">on a glider that\u2019s built for two...</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Wahine tried to hide a blush as she occupied herself with the scenery.<br /> <br /> <i>(perception+awareness roll= 3 successes)</i></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","user":"Foxsimile","date":". 09-08-2014, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T09:19:20-07:00","id":253358,"title":"","content":"&quot;Nyan, you know, those kind of vision never tell you anything useful like that ~&quot; Menreiki nonchalantly answered.<br /> <br /> &quot;Her vision has leaded us to the island, wouldn't hurt to ask, isn't it ?&quot;, the captain seem slightly annoyed at the rabbit-ear man, &quot;I suppose we just have to find a landing spot for ourselves then&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hehheh, we gonna arrive at your hometown at last, are you excited kiddo !&quot;, her master try to lighten up the Maiden's mood with his ama~zing charisma, &quot;Let hope your ancestor are not some giant gorilla's worshiping cannibal tribe, okay&quot;, he continued to talk, &quot;This old cat ship can't support something THAT big&quot;, and talk &quot;Also try to not to make any pacts with demon that will steal your voice, you're the only walking talking translator that we have in case we meet your ancestor, ufufufu~&quot;, and talk, &quot;Double also, have you thought abou....! Nyan !&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Master ! Please be quiet !&quot;, the Maiden pulled at Menreiki's cheek to stop him from bothering her....and everyone else.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ow, ow ow! It's hurt !&quot;, the man began to sob like a baby &quot;Waaaa, I save little girl and she grow up to be an abusive wife !&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;You're being dramatic again, master&quot;, the Maiden let out a long sigh, trying to imagine having to spend weeks with him on an island make her shudder.<br /> <br /> Hmmm, but she is quite curious at the prospect of meeting those that could be her family, should she announce her intention truthfully, and what if they are indeed tribes of crazy Wyld mutant that has demon worship as one of their daily activity like her master said.........<br /> <br /> &quot;Uuuuu, Master, you always make me nervous before important stuffs are about to happen !&quot;<br /> <br /> The Maiden and her master still argued back and forth as the ship approached the island.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i1196.photobucket.com/albums/aa418/crimsonorigami/imagejpg1-15.jpg~original\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 09-10-2014, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T13:49:58-07:00","id":253566,"title":"","content":"The bearer of the bones gritted her teeth \u2013 not a smile, but almost \u2013 and shook her head. &quot;I'm not hungry,&quot; she lied; the youth's courtesy, while not unwelcome, seemed decidedly suspicious. Best she refuse it, as politely as possible.<br /> While Pakari ate, the penitent tended to her charge, painstakingly unraveling each braid on Kusuma's head. She'd done it a thousand times and more, now, and could do it without looking, so she kept her unnecessarily intense stare on her... guest, so to speak.<br /> <br /> &quot;Whence came you?&quot; she asked suddenly, seeing a rare opportunity for small talk. &quot;No village, certainly, or you'd gone by the river.&quot;<br /> The mummy's hair unbraided, she took out a small wooden comb and set to work. It was her habit to neglect her own hair in favour of Kusuma's, as payment for her unwarranted loyalty. She did not mind that it made her seem even more like a witch \u2013 in fact, she derived some strange pleasure from it, not that it seemed to affect <i>this</i> youth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T16:47:45-07:00","id":253669,"title":"","content":"Pakari's initial uncertainty about the Bearer was growing into a mild discomfort. She didn't seem hostile, but the way she worked on the mummy-child's hair without taking her eyes off him was somewhat unnerving. He tried to focus on eating the other half of the meat she had refused, but that ended when she asked where he had come from. He swallowed quickly and answered &quot;from the mountain.&quot; He pointed north. &quot;My master, Hasya, is there, going over the wards on a tomb. Some of them got battered a bit by the last storm, and we have to replace them. We didn't have any bone or Whitestone though, so I'm going to Dreaming River to get some.&quot;<br /> <br /> Pakari paused to stuff the last of the meat into his mouth and closed his eyes while he chewed. &quot;'e altho 'eed 'ope,&quot; he said absently, mouth still full, as he recalled his shopping list. &quot;Ink, 'alth, intenth thickth, an' 'aybe 'ait-traffs-&quot; Pakari swallowed, then continued, eyes still shut. &quot;-in case we need to sacrifice something.&quot; Those were the necessities - Pakari thought he might also get more herbs and spices or a new knife while he was in town, but the job only required some basic ritual ingredients.<br /> <br /> After a second of hesitation, he opened his eyes, and confirmed with some dismay that she was still looking straight at him and combing the child's hair. It was just as bad as before, and Pakari began considering ways that he could politely escape from her company. &quot;So, what are you doing out here?&quot; he asked. It seemed like a safely reciprocal kind of question to ask at this point in the conversation, and would lead very naturally to something like, &quot;Oh, it sounds like you're busy, I should go.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T10:27:13-07:00","id":261355,"title":"","content":"Pakari's food-choked words had brought a proper smile to the bonebearer's face \u2013 being well-versed in the art herself, the sound brought on nostalgia \u2013 but it was already gone.<br /> &quot;Nothing,&quot; she replied, finally taking her eyes off the youth. Kusuma's hair was to be re-braided, and this she needed her eyes to do.<br /> &quot;So,&quot; she continued, &quot;you are a Guardian.&quot; She'd recognized that name, Hasya.<br /> <br /> Braiding Kusuma's hair was the favourite part of her day, in the sense that it was the one constant distraction from the bitter world and bitter gods, but she found the rare conversation better. Best she enjoy it while she could \u2013 at the boy's expense, if necessary.<br /> &quot;Surely the girls of your village are displeased.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T12:50:47-07:00","id":263034,"title":"","content":"<b>Calm Sea Village, RY 67, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> Faruma Black Eyes frowned. &quot;A new chance to sit here and eat cold food and not get to talk to anyone...but yeah. Thanks. Say, I don't suppose you guys could get a guy a flute? I am incredibly bored in here, I might as well practice a bit.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I could probably manage that.&quot; Nemoai shrugged. &quot;Little music in here couldn't hurt, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Give me a Perception+Awareness Roll please, Hapless. Difficulty 2 to hear it, Difficulty 3 to notice the distant sound of the watchtowers along the southern shore sounding an alarm (not the big gong that indicates they've spotted a monster coming in from the sea, but the low horns that mean they've spotted an unknown ship) and react before anyone else does.</i> <i>Feel free to react as appropriate.</i><br /> <br /> <b>High Above Whitestone Island, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half An Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> Seskan was apparently devoting most of his attention to flying without making any mistakes, and Haku was...well, a little distracted by the tips of Wahine's ears turning slightly pink as the bird sang its song. Therefore, it was Wahine, entranced by the beauty of the world spread out below her, who first spotted the ship.<br /> <br /> She knew right away that it wasn't from Whitestone Island. She'd traveled all over the place, and she'd helped build more than a few ships, after all. People here made big canoes for river travel, or built platforms between two hulls for blue-water vessels. The Sunset Tribe tended towards smaller vessels with a smaller draft, the Green Flower Tribe liked larger vessels including a few three-hulled ships with some reinforcements for coastal raiding, and the Dreaming River Tribe was full of slow-moving river-barges with living spaces and huts built onto their platforms...but this ship was the size of a whale, with one huge hull and multiple stories. She could tell just by looking at the wake that it had a huge draft, this thing was designed for the ocean and couldn't handle rivers or even shallower coastal waters.<br /> <br /> The rigging was full of men scurrying up and down managing the sails, and the deck bustled with activity. There were a lot of people on this strange ship.<br /> <br /> <b>On the Deck of the Guild Ship Blue Lily, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour after Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> &quot;No need to worry about the locals,&quot; Captain Phi Ho declared. &quot;My men can handle themselves if things go badly. We have enough arrows to turn a fang of elephants into pincushions, and this far West we've all got something sharp made of iron on us, just in case. That's without even mentioning our ballista, or the firedust bombs we've got stored below in case of pirates. Hopefully the locals will be friendly, discovering a new port willing to trade is much more profitable than finding an island full of angry cannibals, but you need not worry yourself about your safety, young lady. We can handle that.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Captain!&quot; A voice called down from the crow's nest. &quot;Ships ahead! A bunch of little catamarans, look like fishing boats to me, up and down the coast. No flags, but some of 'em look like they've spotted us, they're turning away and heading for land.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Give me a Perception+Awareness Roll, please. Difficulty 3 to notice the gliders circling high over the island. From here they'll just look like triangles, possibly some sort of huge and weirdly angular bird. Difficulty 4 to see from this incredible distance that they're actually gliders with humans hanging from them.</i><br /> <br /> <b>In the Jungle About One Day's Hike from Dreaming River Village, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Shortly After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> As the Bearer of Bones enjoyed Pakari's discomfort, the young man noticed the little forest spirits that had been watching them from the leaves suddenly startle and widen their eyes and scamper off to vanish into solid tree trunks or the dappled green expanse of the canopy like mice startled by a loud noise.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Both of you: Perception+Awareness roll, difficulty 1, to notice the birds have stopped singing and the bugs have stopped chirping.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T13:33:51-07:00","id":263053,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;Nothing,&quot;</i> was the Bearer's answer, and Pakari mentally kicked himself for not coming up with a better question. What had he expected? That a homeless wanderer would constantly be occupied with work or lead an active social life? At least she wasn't staring at him anymore - that was a relief.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;So, you are a Guardian. Surely the girls of your village are displeased.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Pakari's feeling of relief left him immediately as his face flushed and he struggled to regain his mental balance.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The truth was, Pakari didn't really know what to do with women. When he was much younger, the girls in his village had teased him for being so large. When they'd all grown up a bit, they still teased him, but their tenor had changed and he felt ambivalent about that. Nothing his aunt or any other adult figure in his life had taught included how men should relate to women. The girls' attention was flattering, but he didn't know how to respond to it, and when Pakari didn't know what to do he tended to act defensively. Trying to be respectful and considerate to everyone failed miserably in the face of pre-adult drama. Other boys his age were no help. Most of them were also teasing him or openly jealous of the unwanted attention he got. The rest usually gave him advice to the effect of &quot;you're big enough to take whatever you want, so why not do that?&quot; - which went against the core of Pakari's being.<br /> <br /> Things had gotten far worse after his coming-of-age flight. He drifted, he dove, he lost control, he crashed, and the next thing he remembered was when the fishermen dragged him up out of the water, half-conscious and gripping a giant eel hard enough to crack its bones... and somehow that made him a magnet for every woman of marriageable age in Dreaming River. After some weeks of dodging proposals and trying not to seriously offend anyone, Hasya's arrival and announcement that he wanted an apprentice had seemed unbelievably lucky. It wasn't his only reason, but Pakari jumped at the chance to become a Guardian partly so he could escape without breaking anyone's heart.<br /> <br /> The girls were indeed displeased, of course. One or two had even tried to talk him out of it, but what was done was done.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;Um... Yes, I'm a Guardian. Or a Guardian-to-be, anyway,&quot; said Pakari, unconsciously adjusting his blue sash. Better to just avoid the awkward semi-question entirely... &quot;I started training with Hasya a year ago. It's, uh... it's very rewarding. You're a Guardian too, right? I mean, you've got the cloak...&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>(OOC: Rolled 5, 5, 5, 6, and 7. 1 success)</i><br /> <br /> Pakari stopped talking abruptly when he realized that the background noise of the forest had gone quiet, and the spirits were running away. &quot;Wait... something's coming,&quot; Pakari thought aloud as he started looking around for the cause of the disturbance. He shifted his feet and started rolling his shoulders, unsure if he would need to run or fight. At first, he turned northwards. Hasya had told him to be quick, but surely the disaster he'd vaguely alluded to couldn't have come so soon...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 11-10-2014, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T17:05:01-07:00","id":263261,"title":"","content":"<b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Calm Sea Village, RY 67, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise: </div> </div> </div></b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Faruma Black Eyes frowned. &quot;A new chance to sit here and eat cold food and not get to talk to anyone...but yeah. Thanks. Say, I don't suppose you guys could get a guy a flute? I am incredibly bored in here, I might as well practice a bit.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I could probably manage that.&quot; Nemoai shrugged. &quot;Little music in here couldn't hurt, right?&quot; </div> </div> </div>Fokisi turns his head as if hearing something. &quot;Perhaps Neomai. Please look into it. I need to go look into this the watch towers spotted something and it could be trouble. I don't want to be arriving after the panic starts.&quot; With that said he grabs the old coral navy cutlass he has and belts that on before heading down to the beach to see what the commotion was about. His eyes keen for trouble, or worse panicked people.<br /> <br /> ((Ooc: 2 successes <a href=\"http://dice.brainclouds.net/Result.aspx?ID=9RGFWJ7N\" target=\"_blank\">(Perception 2 + Awareness 0) 7,7</a> ))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T00:23:52-07:00","id":263499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/239065-ic-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign?p=263034#post263034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>High Above Whitestone Island, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half An Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> Seskan was apparently devoting most of his attention to flying without making any mistakes, and Haku was...well, a little distracted by the tips of Wahine's ears turning slightly pink as the bird sang its song. Therefore, it was Wahine, entranced by the beauty of the world spread out below her, who first spotted the ship.<br /> She knew right away that it wasn't from Whitestone Island. She'd traveled all over the place, and she'd helped build more than a few ships, after all. People here made big canoes for river travel, or built platforms between two hulls for blue-water vessels. The Sunset Tribe tended towards smaller vessels with a smaller draft, the Green Flower Tribe liked larger vessels including a few three-hulled ships with some reinforcements for coastal raiding, and the Dreaming River Tribe was full of slow-moving river-barges with living spaces and huts built onto their platforms...but this ship was the size of a whale, with one huge hull and multiple stories. She could tell just by looking at the wake that it had a huge draft, this thing was designed for the ocean and couldn't handle rivers or even shallower coastal waters.<br /> The rigging was full of men scurrying up and down managing the sails, and the deck bustled with activity. There were a lot of people on this strange ship.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wahine stared at the ship for a long moment, stunned by it's size and enamored with its design. The range of such a ship must be incredible. She'd seen a few long haul vessels in her youthful travels but nothing even close to the magnitude and grandeur of the ship below. She strained in her harness to get a better look. Too bad her daypack was secured out of her reach with the rest of the gear they'd hauled up to the cliff face. A viewfinder would be very handy about now. But she could still see the movement of many people below. It seems a ship that size needed just short of an army to crew. She pointed animatedly at the ship but grit her teeth at Haku's persistent silence. She whistled to her bird.<br /> <br /> <i><b>There's a large foreign ship down there.</b> </i> She signed with an outstretched hand for her bird to see, mouthing the words along with her signing. She couldn't turn her head enough to look Haku in the eye and mouth out a simple message to his face.<br /> <br /> &quot;Strange ship below Cap'n!&quot; There was a pause. She could almost feel his lips stretching into a smile against her neck as his breath warmed her ears. She gave him a jab in the ribs with her elbow. &quot;No time for kiss kissy!&quot; Her bird reprimanded. &quot;Strange ship! Invaders! Pirates! Scurvy Dogs!&quot; He continued to ad-lib while Haku got his wits about him.<br /> <br /> <i><b>There are a lot of people down there. </b></i> &quot;There's a lot of people down there.&quot; Her bird relayed more clearly, putting aside jokes to better message for his mistress.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Go take a closer look. </b></i> She pointed down towards the largest clump of people among the foreign party. <i><b>See who looks important.</b></i><br /> <br /> &quot;Going down to check it out&quot; He affirmed and banked downward to find a perch someplace close to the action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","user":"Foxsimile","date":". 09-23-2014, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T09:59:28-07:00","id":263892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/239065-ic-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign?p=263034#post263034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>On the Deck of the Guild Ship Blue Lily, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour after Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> &quot;No need to worry about the locals,&quot; Captain Phi Ho declared. &quot;My men can handle themselves if things go badly. We have enough arrows to turn a fang of elephants into pincushions, and this far West we've all got something sharp made of iron on us, just in case. That's without even mentioning our ballista, or the firedust bombs we've got stored below in case of pirates. Hopefully the locals will be friendly, discovering a new port willing to trade is much more profitable than finding an island full of angry cannibals, but you need not worry yourself about your safety, young lady. We can handle that.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Captain!&quot; A voice called down from the crow's nest. &quot;Ships ahead! A bunch of little catamarans, look like fishing boats to me, up and down the coast. No flags, but some of 'em look like they've spotted us, they're turning away and heading for land.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Give me a Perception+Awareness Roll, please. Difficulty 3 to notice the gliders circling high over the island. From here they'll just look like triangles, possibly some sort of huge and weirdly angular bird. Difficulty 4 to see from this incredible distance that they're actually gliders with humans hanging from them.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>The Maiden and her master feel like an outcaste in the ship, what with everyone preparing to approach the island frantically and the two just have to sit around since neither have any knowledge on sailing and such.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Even though the captain has told us to take it easy and enjoy the view I still want to help, just staring at the sky and the sea make me so bore</i>.&quot;, the Maiden complain with her usual nonchalantly voice and the unchanging aloof expression.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Only me and that idiotic tiger know Old Realm on the ship you know, how are you gonna help if you can't even understand the instruction</i>&quot;, Merenki replied &quot;Beside, it seem that there are indeed people on those islands, and they don't seem to be evil cannibal either from the description of the sailor&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Hmmm, I still don't know what to say when we meet the islander yet. Do you think that we should just straight out tell them our intention ?</i>&quot;, the Maiden tilted her head to one side while still keeping a stoic face.<br /> <br /> Her master pondered for a second and give her the answer with star in his eyes, &quot;<i>Aye, nothing is impossible with my supernatural swagness and your uncanny cuteness, so I say we just tell them exactly what we want !</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Mereiki's bravado does make the situation seem optimistic. Let's hope seeing the future is one of his God-Blooded's power package.<br /> <br /> Looking at the island, she felt a moment of calm surrounded her heart, kinda like the stillness before the stor..........nah, she's sure that nothing out of the ordinary will happen, thinking about future omen just make you nervous anyway.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: I rolled [3,4,6,10], 2 successes. </i><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i1196.photobucket.com/albums/aa418/crimsonorigami/imagejpg1-21.jpg~original\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 09-23-2014, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T03:38:18-07:00","id":265304,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#696969\"><i>(Rolled a six and a five. Heh.)</i></span><br /> <br /> &quot;Only of bones,&quot; grunted the penitent, her voice sharp again. She had expected his curiosity, but not the temerity to <i>ask</i>. &quot;Hasya's less wise a teacher than I <i>thought</i>, if\u2014&quot;<br /> <br /> She looked up, corpse-hair only half braided, to find the youth Pakari jumping at shadows, and she did not appreciate the interruption. &quot;<i>Sit</i>, son. Lest you were followed, there's no <i>shura</i> hereabout I've not banished, and no fool boys other than you.&quot; Anger, too, had its pleasures. &quot;Son, you fear pigs? It's all pigs here, if they dare approach their own dead.&quot;<br /> The penitent waved angrily with the bone-comb, indicating the remains of her (Pakari's) breakfast. Apparently, the eerie silence of the jungle was lost on her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 10-16-2014, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T09:58:12-07:00","id":266822,"title":"","content":"Seskan was in awe. He couldn't believe how beautiful the world was when he looked at it from above, like a bird. Sure, at first it was painful- when he just jumped, it felt like the glider was about to torn him apart. Yet, the pain helped him to ignore the dread- that nothing has supported him and that he was going to crush into the rocks at the bottom of the cliff. However, once he took control over the glider, both the pain and the dread vanished, being replaced with a child- like joy. That was the same feeling he felt when he have seen his mentor's first spell- that nothing was impossible, and that nothing could have stopped him.<br /> <br /> &quot;It is beautiful!&quot; he screamed, his eyes tearing from both the winds and the fact that for the first time since he was thrown to the sea he felt alive- not just surviving from one day to the other, but truly being alive.When Haku gave the instructions, he simply nodded, waiting to see what other sights will be revealed before him during his first flight. Sure, a part of him reminded him he shouldn't give into his primal joy too much- after all, he was there to practice and learn, but he still couldn't totally shake it off. Every thought about the past or future has vanished, leaving him in an euphoric state. This was why, when he suddenly heard the stupid bird starting to sing some kind of love song, instead of getting annoyed he has started to laugh- maybe that bag of feathers wasn't that bad after all?<br /> <br /> And with that warm feeling in his chest, he followed Haku and the silent woman as they rode the winds together.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://dice.brainclouds.net/Result.aspx?ID=A3WRPM62\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>(perception+awareness roll= 1 successes)</i></span></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 09-27-2014, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T10:13:05-07:00","id":267489,"title":"","content":"<b>Calm Sea Village, RY 67, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> Fokisi's trip to the beach was short: Calm Sea Village was built into the hills overlooking the inlet where the Sunset River met the sea. Several other men and women joined him as he dashed towards the beach, many of them armed with spears or war-clubs studded with white stones or shark teeth.<br /> <br /> &quot;Who do you think it is?&quot; one of them called to another as they ran. &quot;Dreaming River raid?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Could be a merchant from the Green Flower tribe,&quot; somebody called back.<br /> <br /> As the reached the beach, they could see it in the distance. There was a white shape on the southern horizon, sharp-angled sails silhouetted against the dim green of Hungry Island. The men at the watchtowers must have good eyes, it was still very distant and difficult to make out any details...but getting slowly larger.<br /> <br /> The fishing boats out at sea had spotted it too, and they were making their way back towards the village.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Perception+Sail at Difficulty 3 to spot the ship's colors at this distance and recognize that it's a Guild-owned ship. Fokisi's the only one on this beach who knows who the Guild is and what their flags look like. Difficulty 2 to spot a bright but small orange cloud shaped like the local letter for &quot;strange ship&quot; high overhead.</i><br /> <br /> <b>High Above Whitestone Island, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half An Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> Seskan's delightful reverie was interrupted again by Wahine's bird.<br /> <br /> &quot;Strange ship below Cap'n!&quot; it barked. &quot;No time for Kissy! Strange Ship! Invaders! Pirates! Scurvy Dogs!&quot;<br /> <br /> Seskan had no idea what a dog was, but he could see the mute woman pointing and following her finger he could see a ship on the southern horizon, a ship much larger than those of his homeland and much larger than anything he'd since he'd come to Whitestone Island.<br /> <br /> For his part, Haku noticed as soon as Wahine pointed. &quot;Good eyes, Wahine!&quot; he rumbled. &quot;Seskan! Since you want to be one of us, here's a lesson! Normally I'd be patrolling with a squadron of warriors and we'd fly low over the ship to see who they are, and sink them if they're an enemy! We cannot do that today! Instead, we need to let the Chief and his men know about this!&quot;<br /> <br /> He pulled a tube of bamboo from a belt at his side and uncorked it. Wahine experienced a brief and terrible smell as he held it out away from them, and Seskan watched as a thick cloud of red-orange smoke roiled out of the tube to stream into a line behind Haku and Wahine's glider. Haku banked and turned to shape the cloud as it streamed out behind him, and Wahine got to enjoy the sudden lurch of a wide loop.<br /> <br /> &quot;This signal will notify the other gliders in the air that we've spotted a strange ship! Skywatchers back home with let the Chief know within half an hour! Any squadrons on patrol will come to investigate within forty five minutes!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You need to land and warn the Sunset tribe, they're our allies!&quot; Haku called. &quot;It looks like the ship is heading for their lands! If you're having trouble landing, aim for where the Sunset River meets the sea, aim for water deep enough you can slow down running in it for a few yards, don't just smash into it or you'll break the glider! I will go to-wait a minute!&quot;<br /> <br /> Haku paused, uncharacteristically. Was he actually second-guessing himself?<br /> <br /> &quot;Wahine,&quot; he growled lower, so that she could hear and Seskan could not. &quot;Normally I would go scout this ship, fly low over them and figure out who they are, yell back and forth to speak with them, and report back to the Chief. But there's a risk of slingstones or poisoned arrows, and while I would absolutely love a chance to show off for you, there's not much point in that if somebody puts an arrow in your throat and I'd rather not fly around with a corpse strapped to me for the rest of the morning. Should we risk scouting the ship together, or go with Seskan to warn the Sunset Tribe?&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>On the Deck of the Guild Ship Blue Lily, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour after Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Captain!&quot; called someone from the crow's nest. &quot;There's an...um...an orange cloud up ahead.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What?!&quot; Phi Ho roared. &quot;Wyld-fog?!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No, Captain, much higher...looks like...but that's can't be right...&quot;<br /> <br /> The man in the crow's nest had a telescope, but he didn't really believe what he was seeing. Captain Phi Ho pulled out his own, and stared into it.<br /> <br /> &quot;By the gods,&quot; he growled. &quot;I am going to be so very, very rich...Maiden! I don't suppose you remember whether your people can fly?&quot;<br /> <br /> As he pointed, the Maiden saw a puffy orange cloud against the serene blue of the morning sky above the island. Nobody else on the ship saw anything other than an oddly shaped cloud...but she instantly recognized the character. Somehow she knew it meant &quot;strange ship&quot; in an alphabet she had long ago forgotten...<br /> <br /> <i>Feet pounded on the hot sand. Laughter, not her laughter, but someone else, a young man. The crying of gulls, the sound of waves, the splashing of feet on the cold surf as she chased...who was she chasing? Then, sudden fear. Pain, rough hands, voices yelling in some horrible language, the rattling of irons chains, she reached out for...who was she reaching out for..? A blue sky, and against it black and green sails, huge and dark and horrible, bigger than anything she had ever seen...a ship. A strange ship.</i><br /> <br /> <b>In the Jungle About One Day's Hike from Dreaming River Village, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Shortly After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> As she waved angrily, suddenly the world lurched and the bone comb fell from the Bearer's hand. Pakari stumbled as the ground shook, and all about them was the cracking of tree roots and the thrashing of branches. The stones of the Bearer's improvised firepit rattled and rolled into the ashes, and her spit fell over. In the distance, they heard a huge crash as an old dead tree that had fallen halfway in last night's storm smashed into the ground.<br /> <br /> For about a minute the ground shook, and then there was stillness and a strange, pregnant silence.<br /> <br /> In the distance, tentatively, a bird began to sing. Shortly, others joined it, and the noises of the jungle slowly returned to normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T23:32:27-07:00","id":268035,"title":"","content":"<b>High Above Whitestone Island, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half An Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> At Haku's hesitation and murmured concerns, Wahine pointed downward at her bird who had already descended in the flurry of words and actions.<br /> <br /> <b>I sent the bird</b> She tried to communicate through gestures and signs as she mouthed out the words, hoping he could see her face well enough to read her lips as he navigated. From her position, it was probably much easier for him to look at her than the other way around. <b> He can get close. He's the perfect spy.</b><br /> <br /> <i>***OOC Just in case: made a roll to communicate her message. Made a guess at what roll to make. Charisma+linguistics or Charisma+ socialize are the same dice pool for me. Rolled 1 success.***</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Guild Ship Blue Lily, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour after Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> The ashen bird flew a few lazy circles around the ship, tightening his circle as he descended and wove in and out of the paths of coastal seabirds bobbing about in the morning air. He took up a spot on the rope netting where he could observe the activity of the ship. Other than the occasional seagull trying to nose in on his space, it was a central place to watch the activity of the ship and maybe catch some snippets of conversation.<br /> <br /> <br /> (<i>If you want the bird to roll something, any bird creature template will do. Other than being exceptionally intelligent, he's just a bird </i>)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","user":"Foxsimile","date":". 09-29-2014, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T10:55:35-07:00","id":268348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>On the Deck of the Guild Ship Blue Lily, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour after Sunrise:</b> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Kiddo, wake up!&quot; Merenki tried to snap the Maiden out of her trance when she saw the orange smoke in the sky.<br /> <br /> &quot;Eh...what...just happen...&quot; who is the person in that vision, she thought to herself for just a moment when she noticed her master worried look &quot;Don't worry Master, it just another weird vision&quot;.<br /> <br /> He gave her a light nod &quot;Just don't do that again, you're almost make me want to wet my pant in front of everybody&quot;, it's seem that one of the perk of speaking Old Realm is that not many would care when you say stuff like Merenki.<br /> <br /> The Maiden stared at her master for a second or two when the Captain dragged both master and student to reality &quot;Maiden, the smoke seem to spell some word, can you confirm this for me ?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Ah...ah, my apologize for dazing out like that. Hmm, it's kinda hard to look at, but I think the word seem to be <i>strange ships</i>.&quot; the Maiden flustered as she answer the Captain's question, now that she think about, she never remember ever encounter these syllables in her journey....Could that mean....<br /> <br /> &quot;Wha....what ! does that mean the islander have already know about our ship ! What should we do ! What should we do ! Ahhhhhh&quot;, Merenki began to run around in circle with both his hands in the air, an activity dubbed by the Maiden as the turkey dance, &quot;Master, calm down ! You are damaging everybody morale with your weird movement !&quot;, she screamed and tried to grappled her master with her whole body. Past experiences has showed her that when her Master began to panic, she just needed to hug him for a minute, it's has been working effectively so far,<br /> <br /> When the Maiden managed to stopped Merenki's tantrum she turned to the Captain &quot;The islander will probably not welcome us, what should we do now, Captain ?&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i1196.photobucket.com/albums/aa418/crimsonorigami/imagejpg1-23.jpg~original\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T12:00:38-07:00","id":268425,"title":"","content":"Seskan has waited patiently as his two teachers discussed about the new situation. While he couldn't hear them, he could understand that the two were trying to decide what should their next actions would be- especially after the mute woman has sent her bird toward the boat. while waving her hands in some weird gestures. That gave him some time to think about his position in the situation- or more exactly, what he could gain from it.<br /> <br /> First, he noted himself to research the &quot;firestick&quot; Haku has used. While he has known that certain materials may burn spontaneously, the exact formula has interested him- so he should find the one who made those and learn his or her secrets. After that, he has started to think more deeply about the situation- from what Haku has said, there may or may not a battle coming ahead, which he assumed to be the main reason he wished to send him away. He agreed with that line of thought- he was a supporter, not a fighter, and while dying for &quot;his people&quot; would probably make them see him as one of them, he would still be dead- something he preferred to avoid. However, sending him alone was not that much better- he while he enjoyed flying, he wasn't sure that he could land good enough (just the thought about it made his stomach twitch). It would be much better if someone was to escort him..<br /> <br /> But, that was only the risk. What about the gain? Even if the main reason for him going away was to get rid of him, if he could land the glider without harm, go to the Sunset tribe and warn them from an upcoming enemy, it would greatly assist him in gaining the respect and appreciation of his own tribe, and may even impress Haku enough to make him ally! Sure, there was a risk (like, that for example, he will get lost, or maybe that the Sunset tribe won't listen to him), but the thought about all of the people look at him as some kind of an hero in stand of a foreigner (or worse, as was in hims homeland), has charmed him enough to attempt and take it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Time is not by our side!&quot; he called toward Haku &quot;If the ship is really an enemy, we should try and warn our allies as fast as we can! Wouldn't it be the best for me to go already, while you two would supervise the threat?&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>(ooc- tell me if I need to role social combat or something. My first game and all :P)</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T13:00:34-07:00","id":268481,"title":"","content":"<b>On the Deck of the Guild Ship Blue Lily, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour after Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> The excitable rabbit eared man caught the bird's attention and curiosity. After a stretch and a puff of his feathers he inched down the rope netting of his mast as the rabbit man flailed his arms about, stopping within a few feet above the height of the crew on the deck. He squawked and chittered a bit as parrots tend to do in the morning hours as he edged downward.<br /> <br /> &quot;The islander will probably not welcome us, what should we do now, Captain ?&quot;<br /> <br /> About that moment, the stocky parrot fluttered the rest of the way down and landed with a little bit of a heavy thud on the wooden deck in front of the rabbit man and the girl by his side. He fluffed his feathers, gave his red tail a good swish, and cocked his head at the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T13:08:18-07:00","id":268488,"title":"","content":"Whatever response Pakari might have given to the Bearer's comments was forgotten when he experienced the worst earthquake of his life.<br /> <br /> When the ground stopped shaking, Pakari took a moment to steady his legs and his nerves. He had never felt the earth rumble like that before - the tiny quakes in the southern part of the island were nothing by comparison. Again, Pakari looked northwards, wondering if some terrible monster or fearsome magic had gotten loose and was now destroying the very land itself.<br /> <br /> Almost as soon as the idea occurred to him, he dismissed it as childish - there was no reason think the world was ending, and if it was there was nothing he could do about it. At a time like this, he had to focus on practical, immediate problems - like his supply run. The quake wouldn't be doing Hasya's improvised wards any favors, and at this point Pakari would help best by retrieving the goods he had been tasked to get, and bringing them back as quickly as he could. If he had survived the quake, and Pakari had no reason to think that he wouldn't, Hasya could certainly take care of himself for a little longer.<br /> <br /> Having made his decision, Pakari checked on The Bearer - she'd been as surprised as he was, he was sure, but she didn't seem to be hurt. &quot;Sorry, I have to go,&quot; he said. He paused, feeling somehow that he needed to explain himself. &quot;I don't know if that quake was from Windrest, but if it was then it's even more important that I get those warding supplies.&quot; He paused again, fighting an instinct to invite her along (which he was sure she would reject) or to stay longer (which he could not afford). Finally, he said &quot;It was nice meeting you,&quot; and awkwardly turned to leave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T11:02:30-07:00","id":269272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Calm Sea Village, RY 67, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> Fokisi's trip to the beach was short: Calm Sea Village was built into the hills overlooking the inlet where the Sunset River met the sea. Several other men and women joined him as he dashed towards the beach, many of them armed with spears or war-clubs studded with white stones or shark teeth.<br /> <br /> &quot;Who do you think it is?&quot; one of them called to another as they ran. &quot;Dreaming River raid?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Could be a merchant from the Green Flower tribe,&quot; somebody called back.<br /> <br /> As the reached the beach, they could see it in the distance. There was a white shape on the southern horizon, sharp-angled sails silhouetted against the dim green of Hungry Island. The men at the watchtowers must have good eyes, it was still very distant and difficult to make out any details...but getting slowly larger.<br /> <br /> The fishing boats out at sea had spotted it too, and they were making their way back towards the village.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Perception+Sail at Difficulty 3 to spot the ship's colors at this distance and recognize that it's a Guild-owned ship. Fokisi's the only one on this beach who knows who the Guild is and what their flags look like. Difficulty 2 to spot a bright but small orange cloud shaped like the local letter for &quot;strange ship&quot; high overhead.</i> </div> </div> </div>That is a pretty big ship to be out that far and be visible. Fokisi can't help but to be reminded of the ships he served on with the coral Navy. He fought back nervousness and stood firm. &quot;Alight people, stay calm, they are still a ways away and they aren't hostile. More than likely it's just people come to trade so let's just keep our heads about us and look like we aren't a bunch of wyld men.&quot; He says to the crowd. &quot;We can disperse a little bit, and wait till they are close enough to come ashore, then we can cluster around them and offer trade.&quot; He is basicly trying to say 'nothing to see here for at least a half an hour people move along.' He worried that someone might start a panic without meaning to as their imagination got the better of them. Best people got busy doing things.<br /> <br /> (( And I don't see a thing <a href=\"http://dice.brainclouds.net/Result.aspx?ID=RJYGDC6D\" target=\"_blank\">Perception 2 + Sail 2 (<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">3,4,5,9</span></span></span>)</a><br /> That might get them to move. <a href=\"http://dice.brainclouds.net/Result.aspx?ID=F3JYCHNL\" target=\"_blank\">Order to disperse (Cha3 + Presence 3 +speciality 1)<br /> (<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">3,4,4,5,5,7,8</span></span></span>)</a> ))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T09:32:09-07:00","id":270166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> About that moment, the stocky parrot fluttered the rest of the way down and landed with a little bit of a heavy thud on the wooden deck in front of the rabbit man and the girl by his side. He fluffed his feathers, gave his red tail a good swish, and cocked his head at the two. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Eh, I didn't realize that we have a pet on the ship ?&quot; said the Maiden when she felt a light breeze appeared behind her and turned back only to see a strange bird that she has never seen before.<br /> <br /> Captain Phi Ho was just as puzzled as the Maiden &quot;It's a parrot, Maiden. And I don't think I ever owned one as far as I know.&quot;, he answered the girl, &quot;But I heard that they mostly lived in tropical place though, I wonder what does a lone bird doing on the sea ?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Heh heh, maybe he want to be the mascot for your ship&quot;, the Maiden playfully responded, she tilted her head to one side and extended her hand so she can pat the exotic creature ,&quot;You travel all this way to do that, didn't you ?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T11:55:56-07:00","id":270259,"title":"","content":"He bowed his head briefly and relented to a quick pet before stepping up onto the girl's outstretched hand. <br /> <br /> &quot;Hiiiii!&quot; he said in Seatongue as well as a string of similar greetings in a variety of languages and voices. He looked back and forth at the crew, chirping a variety of noises and turning his head to the side as he shifted his weight on the maiden's hand.<br /> <br /> &quot;Kitty!&quot; he shouted in Seatounge at Captain Phi Ho. &quot;Meow, Meow!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T20:58:24-07:00","id":270573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Kitty!&quot; he shouted in Seatounge at Captain Phi Ho. &quot;Meow, Meow!&quot; </div> </div> </div>&quot;Huumm, is that Seatongue I heard ?&quot;, the Maiden said out loud while her Master still napping dutifully in her lap, wait, now the Maiden felt like an idiot for asking such a question, bird can't tal....&quot;Yeah, these bird can mimic human language, and he just called me a kitty :sigh: I'm hopping for an <i>awesome captain </i>instead.&quot;, and after the captain answer she kinda wished that she has bought those scrolls about the West geography and biography when they visited An-Teng last summer. <br /> <br /> The Maiden turned her attention back to the bird, her ebony eyes almost gleamed with tiny stars of excitement which are usually concealed by a stoic expression on her face, &quot;Who is the cutest bird of all, yes you are, yes you are !&quot;, the Maiden said this as she slowly moved her hand left and right while the bird wiggled from side to side almost like those colorful gelatinous cube that you usually saw on some the Southerner food stand.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T22:11:35-07:00","id":270615,"title":"","content":"He blew a raspberry at the Captain then puffed his feathers at the Maiden's affectionate tone, bowing his head for a scratch. When he'd had enough attention, he fluttered back up to the rigging and started milling about, scooting back and forth and up and down the ropes. He mouthed the slipknots of the ship's rigging, picking at loose threads of rope and sailcloth like a mouthy toddler. He gave one of the rigging knots an innocent tug, then another.<br /> <br /> An average bird would know nothing of the nature of a ship's rigging or the peculiarities of sailor's knots. But he was far from an average bird.<br /> <br /> &quot;What's this?&quot; he sang as he toddled back and forth along the boom of the main mast, chewing on an important looking rope with his can-opener of a beak, popping about half of the threads before getting bored. &quot;What's this? What's this?&quot; He sang again, hopping over pick at the halyards (lines that pull sails up and down the mast).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","user":"Foxsimile","date":". 10-02-2014, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T11:27:19-07:00","id":270968,"title":"","content":"The Maiden seem very occupied with the parrot, teenager girl are weak to feather and fur after all. As she was marveling at the bird's childlike behaviors she suddenly sensed a wave of......jealousy emitting from her Master.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, this ship already has a mascot, hasn't it ?&quot;, well, it's not surprise that someone like Merenki would welcome a rival, &quot;And why does a tropical creature would ventured all its way to the ocean anyway. Get it off the ship already or you gonna has seven years of bad luck ahead of you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Again, the captain is the one who have to pull both of them back to reality again, &quot;So, Maiden .....about our plan when we finally meet the friendly local....&quot;, he cough and then continued &quot;I'm not exactly a person guy so I suppose I should let you two decide our next course of action.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;E....eh, sorry captain for being distracted again&quot;, the girl blushed, if this keep happened then her pride as a responsible adult will soon be shattered into the void, and now about captain Phi Ho's question, &quot;Since they have already knew about our arrival there will probably be people with pointy things waiting for us at the shore...&quot;, the black-haired girl calmly explained her thought, &quot;...but I think some warm greeting from us and then proceed to announcing our intention truthfully should diffuse the situation quickly enough to sway the islander to our goal.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T19:30:29-07:00","id":271289,"title":"","content":"He squawked loudly from his perch above everyone's heads. &quot;What's the plan Cap'n!&quot; he screeched in Seatongue. &quot;What's the plan! Plan Plan! Captain! Here kitty kitty...&quot; He bounced up and down, parroting the voices of an assortment people he'd come across over the years. &quot;Intensions! Intensions? To arms my good men! Good sir, good sir... what are your intensions? Shall we stay the course? To the boats!&quot; He continued to babble in between hints of intelligible conversation, speaking mostly in a variety of Seatongue dialects with sprinkling of words in the local island's language and the occasional random word of foul mouthed flame tongue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T00:05:07-07:00","id":272088,"title":"","content":"&quot;Our goal here is to establish a trade route so fighting the islander will, of course, be a bad idea.&quot;, the Captain stroke his chin with one hand while still trying to think about any surprising problem that may emerge when they finally reach the island, &quot;Not to mention it will be hard for you to conduct your investigation if the local are all hostile to us. Speaking of that, Maiden, what are your plan concerning the vision in your dream if we manage to stay there ?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Investigation sound a little.......serious, Captain.&quot;, the girl cough, &quot;But...eh....I honestly not sure what to do about it myself, just asking people if they know me don't really sound like a good idea. And I have a feeling that mentioning my vision will result in a me being chased around by the local, don't you think ?&quot;<br /> <br /> Both the raven-haired girl and the tiger-headed man nodded there head in agreement, &quot;I suppose we will just have to deal with the local first, having them being friendly to us will certainly make it easier for your...heh...investigation.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T00:50:21-07:00","id":279433,"title":"","content":"<b>High Above Whitestone Island, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half An Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> &quot;The bird will be able to find you again if we land?&quot; Haku seemed impressed. &quot;Clever creature. Too bad they take so long to train, they'd make excellent messengers...Calm yourself, Seskan!&quot;<br /> <br /> Haku banked to face away from the ship, back towards the island.<br /> <br /> &quot;Our gliders are much faster than any ship! But you're right, we should warn our allies. I'm going to land first! Follow alongside me and copy what I do exactly! Taking off and landing are the most dangerous parts of flying, so if you're going to get yourself killed today it'll be in about three minutes when we land! We'll be landing in water, and you don't want to get trapped under your glider and drown, so once you've come to a stop pull the cord to release your harness!&quot;<br /> <br /> Over the next couple of minutes, Haku and Wahine made a long slow descent from the sky over the ocean towards the mouth of the Sunset River. As the river grew rapidly larger, Wahine experienced an instinctive lurch in her stomach and rush of adrenaline simliar to when they'd first taken off: falling slowly and at an angle is, when you get close enough to the ground, still falling. The white sand of the beach swelled in size before her, and the tiny people gathered on it grew bigger and bigger and suddenly they were behind her-Haku tilted the glider upward slightly and ran along the surface of the water, and all she could see was his feet and splashing foam. The glider soared perpendicular to the surface of the river, and slowly Haku's rapidly pumping legs sank deeper into it...<br /> <br /> &quot;Take a deep breath!&quot; Haku yelled, and suddenly they were underwater and the world was roiling bubbles and her pounding heart and the terrifying realization that it's very hard to swim when strapped to a man twice your size, and then her head broke the surface as that powerful man treaded water for the both of them. The glider floated in the river about a yard away, drifting gently out towards the ocean. Haku grabbed one of its straps and looked upward. Ignoring Wahine for the moment, he bellowed skyward.<br /> <br /> &quot;Don't get too deep too fast, or you'll flip over and break the wings!&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Seskan, it's a Dex+Ride roll to make a controlled descent from your current altitude down to the river. It's a second Dex+Ride roll to land in the river, and no untrained penalties or anything due to previous tutelage from Alial. The Difficulty for the first roll is 1. The Difficulty for the second roll is 3. You get a two-die bonus for Haku's tutelage: guy just rocked a masterful success on his own rolls. If you fail the roll for the descent, the difficulty for the landing will increase to 4. Each success beyond the threshold on your first roll will decrease the difficulty for landing by one, to a minimum of one. Failure on the landing will result in damage to the glider. A botch on the descent increases landing difficulty to 5, and a botch on the landing roll will result in damage to your character. Feel free to make the roll to descend first: knowing how well the descent roll went will let you know whether you want to spend Willpower or channel a Virtue on the landing roll.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Calm Sea Village, RY 67, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> Fokisi's voice quieted the crowd.<br /> <br /> &quot;You're right, of course,&quot; a woman said. Fokisi recognized her: Leilo Sweet-Tide, the woman who had sent the basket of yams to his jailhouse this morning. &quot;Hey, everyone, if they're here to trade and we're all standing around like children who've never seen a big boat before, they'll think we never get any business and offer us shit prices!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Good point!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;We should probably bargain as a group! That way they can't play us off against each other.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Fair, fair...but we can't all stand around squabbling, we'll look like pushovers. Somebody needs to be in charge.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Should we get the tribal elder?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Nah, Green Hands is half deaf. We should get the priest!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm flattered,&quot; the priest spoke up, &quot;but that ship doesn't look like it's from around here. If Fokisi's stories about distant lands are true, they worship strange gods and they speak in strange tongues. It should be Fokisi who speaks to them, their ship looks similar to the one which brought him here, he might know their language. And besides, if they're hostile, having our representative be a strong young warrior is a better idea than an old healer like myself. It shows strength.&quot;<br /> <br /> There was much nodding, and the crowd began to slowly disperse and get back to acting as best they could like big foreign ships weren't really anything special.<br /> <br /> &quot;If they are looking for a fight,&quot; one of the young men said, &quot;shouldn't we get ready for it? Maybe keep some men up in those trees with spears, where they can't be seen from the water?&quot;<br /> <br /> About this time, Neomai caught up, panting. &quot;What...what's going on? Why is everybody-&quot;<br /> <br /> With a tremendous splash a man with a woman strapped to him and giant wings of canvas and laquer painted to look like a great sea-hawk suddenly came down out of the sky and ran along the surface of the water for about fifty yards before sinking to a perfect landing in the bay.<br /> <br /> After a brief pause in which everyone stared like idiots, the man and his passenger resurfaced next to their floating glider and bellowed, &quot;&quot;Don't get too deep too fast, or you'll flip over and break the wings!&quot;<br /> <br /> A second glider was coming in behind the first.<br /> <br /> <b>On the Deck of the Guild Ship Blue Lily, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour after Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Um, Captain Phi Ho?&quot; The cabin boy spoke up a little nervously. &quot;Somebody trained that parrot, and, well, parrots just repeat whatever you say. So if there's something you don't want the locals to hear, like about the Maiden and her, um, issues, then maybe us talking about it in front of the parrot would be a...bad idea?&quot;<br /> <br /> There was a brief pause.<br /> <br /> &quot;We could eat 'im.&quot; The ship's cook chimed in. &quot;I know a couple of decent recipes for parrot.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Trained, eh? Like a messenger, you think?&quot; The Captain purred in thought, a deep basso sound which rattled the breakfast tray that had been brought out a few minutes ago. &quot;Parrot! Go tell your master that we come in peace, and that we seek to trade goods and stories! Also, tell your master that while we are friendly we are incredibly well-armed and will defend ourselves viciously if attacked. Now, um...shoo!&quot;<br /> <br /> He moved towards the bird, waving his arms in an attempt to convince it to take off again.<br /> <br /> &quot;They're really quite good,&quot; the cook grumbled. &quot;Especially with a good stuffing and cider...&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>In the Jungle About One Day's Hike from Dreaming River Village, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> As Pakari turned to leave, a gentle breeze began to blow from the direction he'd come from. As he watched, the little spirits that he'd seen hide before the earthquake poked their heads out from behind tree branches and looked at one another...and then uniformly dashed off through the branches like frightened monkeys. Something...he wasn't sure what, but it had long legs and far too many of them and it was about the size of a house...scurried through the distant forest in the same direction. The animals didn't seem to notice, the birds were still chirping...but the local spirits were all fleeing something, and they were all fleeing in the same direction.<br /> <br /> That direction was away from where he'd left Hasya.<br /> <br /> <b>At the Tomb of the Stone Maw, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> The Tomb of the Stone Maw is built into a section of the mountainside that juts out in a large rocky outcropping. The black stone of the mountainside was carved long, long ago into a demonic visage: a face with great bulging eyes and tusks. Its eternally roaring mouth opened in an archway as tall as a man and wide enough for three to walk into it side by side, if they were foolish enough to do so. Its great lolling stone tongue formed a rough ramp leading up into the dark passageway. The whole affair had been draped in vines and coated with moss by the ages, so some of the effect had been lost, but it was still a foreboding sort of place, the sort of place you built explicitly to tell future generations, &quot;Hey. This is a bad scary place that you should not go into.&quot;<br /> <br /> According to the Temple Guardians, the Tomb of the Stone Maw had been built by the gods themselves to house the body of a horrible criminal. The stories varied: records from the Dreaming River's oldest temples indicated the tomb belonged to a dark sorcerer, a sea-wizard who had summoned storms and terrible waves and who had commanded dark spirits to bedevil the people of the island. They said he'd been struck down by the gods for his crimes. The Green River Tribe's priests claimed the tomb was the resting place of one of Keshet's children, a half-god chieftain of their people who had turned into a monster and devoured his own family before vanishing into the jungle. They said he had stalked and devoured young men and women from all over the island, and that Keshet's grief at his son's madness had led to three years of unrelenting rain before the beast was slain. The Sunset Tribe claimed that the tomb housed a god slain in battle against an army of demons, and said that the other gods had built the tomb to honor his memory, and had filled it with curses and surrounded it with warnings to prevent it being defiled by the presence of mortals. The Whispering Valley Tribe claimed the tomb had been built by Konani of the Evening Light to house a terrible witch with whom he had fallen in love but had slain anyway to protect his people from her fell magic.<br /> <br /> The only thing everybody agreed on was that the gods had summoned a guardian to stop any prying mortals from disturbing the eternal rest of the one who slept in this tomb, and that the guardian was terrifying: it was invincible in battle and enjoyed devouring humans, and it never slept. Its claws could rend stone and its breath was a black cloud that blotted out the light of the sun, and even the gods feared its dread power. This was fine...until several centuries ago a foolish priest had entered the tomb and stolen something. The guardian had retaliated by coming out of the tomb every night of the New Moon after that, devouring anyone it could catch. It had been sealed away again after three bloody years by the personal intercession of the gods on behalf High Priest at the time, and he had given his life in the binding of the monster. For hundreds of years the priests had maintained the wards keeping it locked away in the tomb where it belonged.<br /> <br /> The wards in question included the annual sacrifice of a white goat at the entrance of the tomb, sigils carved into the trees surrounding the tomb and painted over with pig's blood on the day before each night of the New Moon, and sacred chimes hanging all around the entrance which thrummed in deep wooden tones when the wind brushed them against each other. Unfortunately, the big storm last night had downed two of those sigil-bearing trees, and had torn down about half of the sacred wind chimes along with them, breaking several in the process. Hasya had sent Pakari to gather supplies to replace them. The New Moon was six days away.<br /> <br /> Hasya was feeling pretty pleased with himself despite the situation. He'd managed to get most of the chimes strung back up, and they were once again thrumming pleasantly. He'd carved sigils into some more trees surrounding the area to match the ones on the fallen trees...he wasn't sure they'd work until Pakari came back with the pig's blood to paint onto them, but he figured it was better than nothing. He was just sitting back and stretching his aching back (he was getting too old to be climbing trees to hang ropes, he decided) when the birds of the forest went abruptly silent.<br /> <br /> A moment later, the earth rumbled, and the trees shook violently, and the ground rippled like waves at sea, and the stone tongue of the Tomb of the Stone Maw splintered and cracked, and he lost his footing and fell to the earth and banged his hip, and two more trees weakened by the storm creaked and crashed to the ground, and the wind chimes along with them.<br /> <br /> Then there was another deep, still silence.<br /> <br /> And from the shadows within the Stone Maw, a scraping sound like an obsidian knife being sharpened on stone, and a deep rumbling chuckle.<br /> <br /> &quot;Today is really not your day, old priest.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 10-13-2014, 04:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T09:11:23-07:00","id":281106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>On the Deck of the Guild Ship Blue Lily, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour after Sunrise:</b> </div> </div> </div>The captain look at Merenki with a strange expression, as if something was wriggling in his mouth from the Maiden's point of view, &quot;Even an idiot is right once in a blue moon, eh ?&quot;, the tiger of the ocean signed and spoke out his thought .<br /> <br /> &quot;Hmm, is something the matter my Captain ?&quot;, the Maiden puzzled as she tilted her head to one side and putting one finger to her cheek, is this one of those &quot;tsundere&quot; moment that she have read in <i>The Live and Romance of Mars </i>she wondered.<br /> <br /> &quot;Wh.....what, the parrot is a sp..........uuummmmm..&quot;, captain Phi Ho covered the Maiden's mouth after he explained to her about the possibility of the strange bird being sent by the islander.<br /> <br /> Giving a sideway look the bird she removed the captain's paw and whispered &quot;Does the local even speak Old Realm, and I don't think they will figure out our plan with just a few disconnected words from that bird, I think......&quot;, cursed it, first it's magic vision, then flying people and now it's some kind of secret agent bird, this journey just getting stranger and stranger every minute.<br /> <br /> &quot;Nyan, this may be a good time for some rehearsal, don't you think ?&quot;, Merenki spoke as he letting out a big yawn.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ah, I almost forgot that I'm the only spoke-woman of this ship, captain Phi Ho, what kind of stuff are we going to trade with the islander ?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T14:58:03-07:00","id":281507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/239065-ic-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign?p=279433#post279433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>High Above Whitestone Island, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half An Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Seskan, it's a Dex+Ride roll to make a controlled descent from your current altitude down to the river. It's a second Dex+Ride roll to land in the river, and no untrained penalties or anything due to previous tutelage from Alial. The Difficulty for the first roll is 1. The Difficulty for the second roll is 3. You get a two-die bonus for Haku's tutelage: guy just rocked a masterful success on his own rolls. If you fail the roll for the descent, the difficulty for the landing will increase to 4. Each success beyond the threshold on your first roll will decrease the difficulty for landing by one, to a minimum of one. Failure on the landing will result in damage to the glider. A botch on the descent increases landing difficulty to 5, and a botch on the landing roll will result in damage to your character. Feel free to make the roll to descend first: knowing how well the descent roll went will let you know whether you want to spend Willpower or channel a Virtue on the landing roll.</i>he trees shook violently, and the ground rippled like waves at sea, and the stone tongue of the Tomb of the Stone Maw splintered and cracked, and he lost his f.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seskan looked on how his teachers flew toward the ground, trying to analyze their every move. While a part of him was sadden that apparently Haku has decided to go with him- his rational part has quickly took over. After all, he saw the very fact that he was flying as a miracle. After that, he was so busy at enjoying it until he forgot from the fact he should return to the ground one day. Even Haku and the silent woman, who has had years of experience at flying, didn't made it look easy. There was a strong possibility he would actually die. He quickly shook his head, not willing to give into the bad thoughts- he had to stay focused. It was just like his mentor has taught him- give in to the Dream, and your mind would break. Let the mind break, and your body would break. Make your body into an iron, and the Dream would go away.<br /> <br /> Slowly, following the Haku's instructions, Seskan has started to lose height. The ground has started to come closer and closer, while the air pressure and the wind shocked his body- but he managed to maintain control over the glider. He navigated himself toward the river, watching the shimmering water who danced beneath him.. and that's where things has gone wrong.<br /> <br /> He wasn't sure what has happened- maybe his legs hit the water too soon? Or perhaps he did a wrong movement with the glider? Whatever the reason was, once he hit the water he has suddenly lost control over the all process. He felt the air pulling his arms up, while the water tries to take him down. For a second, he was sure he was going to be torn into two, when finally the air and the water seemed to get into an agreement that he should stay down. He fell into the water, while thankfully the river has soften the crush a bit. After a few moments in which he managed to regain control over himself and pulled himself to the shore, he freed himself from the cursed glider, noticing he was damaged by his fall. Sure, Alail may get angry on him- but he'll make him up for that later. Besides, he would understand it is better the glider than him.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well,&quot; he said to Haku with a smile while swallowing a curse or true &quot;that was fun. Should we get going?&quot;<br /> <br /> (<a href=\"http://dice.brainclouds.net/Result.aspx?ID=PYM6RLHB]23(4d10) = 23\" target=\"_blank\">first </a>Dex+Ride 2 successes, <a href=\"http://dice.brainclouds.net/Result.aspx?ID=MJWYVC6J]19(4d10) = 19\" target=\"_blank\">second </a>1 successes. Apparently, I should have had spent willpower :P)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T19:37:02-07:00","id":283118,"title":"","content":"Signaling to the glider users Fokisi runs over and looks to the people who just landed in his harbor. He makes brief notice of the woman before looking at the glider scouts with a calmness about him of someone who has seen adversity throughout his life and lived to tell the tale. &quot;Do you need help?&quot; When it became obvious that Seskan was able to handle himself Fokisi motions to them as a whole to come closer so that they can speak more in private without being over heard. &quot;Anything you can tell me of this ship? People are a bit nervous, and I would be happy to tell them it's just traders.&quot; He looks at these ones who make their lives like the sea hawk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T12:50:07-07:00","id":284061,"title":"","content":"Pakari started walking, then stopped dead in his tracks as he looked down and around him. Tiny ethereal creatures ran past him and away from him, fading from view as they fled into the bush. In his experience, it was pretty rare for the spirits to flee from anything. Most creatures could not see them or touch them - the only thing they really had to fear was other spirits. Malevolent spirits.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, Moana's tits&quot;, said Pakari, possibly a little louder than he intended. He turned around again and started walking back north, passing the Bearer, then stopped again. Part of him wanted to sprint to Hasya's side, but he had no idea what kind of trouble his master might be in or what he might be rushing into. He had no supplies, no weapons, and no time to think. He looked back over his shoulder at the Bearer, then turned to face her. She did have that sword... could she help?<br /> <br /> No, there was no time to talk. Pakari let out an exasperated breath and turned north again. He started walking, then jogging, and then finally running off into the jungle, heading back to the Tomb of the Stone Maw as quickly as he could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 10-16-2014, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T14:42:56-07:00","id":284225,"title":"","content":"When the youth Pakari hurried away \u2013 the first time, that is \u2013 the Bearer nodded sagely at his back. Doubtless the earthquake had frightened him, as it would've frightened <i>her</i> in her youth, before she had joined the ranks of the stormbirds. When he <i>returned</i>, however...<br /> <br /> In the intervening time, she completed the final braid on Kusuma's head, and pinned up her own matted hair, and rumbled one of her innumerable prayers of penance. Then the youth returned, as quickly as he had gone, gave her a tactless look, and hurried on into the deeper jungle.<br /> She was unused to this \u2013 to people returning \u2013 but that only startled her briefly, for the meaning of things finally dawned on her. Here she was, not far from the Stone Maw (or whichever damned tomb it was), in the wake of thunder on the wind and thunder in the earth; an apprentice of master Hasya had crossed her path, first on some urgent errand and then in dereliction of it.<br /> He seemed like a dutiful boy, too.<br /> <br /> She rose and assembled her meagre things \u2013 swords at her hip, shield at her side, pretty corpse on her back \u2013 and set off after Pakari. ...As quickly and <i>silently</i> as she could, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T14:59:49-07:00","id":284249,"title":"","content":"Seskan looked a the new guy at interest. From the fact he was the one to greet them has showed that apparently he was in charge in the place. Maybe a warrior or an enforcer of some kind- someone to whom the people turned when they needed help. Logically, he knew that he was suppose to side quietly and let Haku do all the talking- but that wasn't what he had in mind. Those people didn't really appreciated weakness, so showing a little attitude could work for his benefit. Sure, Haku may see him as rude and decide he wasn't acting accordingly- but in that case, he could always pull the &quot;stranger&quot; card and apologies for still trying to learn the ways of their people. It worked for him when he met the High Priestess, after all- a win win situation, which could help him rise his reputation, and maybe even gaining someone in a key position as an ally.<br /> <br /> And so, Seskan stepped forward and said &quot;We do not know. From what we saw, the ship isn't like the ones who usually trade in here. Perhaps they are simply merchants or travelers, and maybe they are something more. the dear lady&quot; he said, while turning to the silent woman &quot;in her wisdom, has sent her talking bird as a spy- and when it would return we may discover a thing or two about those who live in the ship&quot; he looked at Haku and continued, directing his words to both his flying teacher and the new guy &quot;If I were to advice you, I would have said that the first to meet the ship should be our soldiers, while we shouldn't do anything hasty- for they may be potential new trade partners, but I do believe my advise is unnecessary for it was your plan, isn't it?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T06:54:14-07:00","id":284917,"title":"","content":"Ignore this post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":".  Accidentally put this in IC instead of OOC 10-17-2014, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T22:19:18-07:00","id":285698,"title":"","content":"Wahine held her breath in the final heart pounding seconds of the decent, bracing for an underwater plunge of indeterminable force. Landing suddenly on the water was thrilling, and when they landed safely in one piece without so much as a chip on the lacquer or scuff on the wing, she let out a riotous laugh though not a sound escaped her beyond great inhales of breath. She quickly popped the buckles holding her against Haku and sought out her assorted small possessions before they floated away or sank. Her whistle managed to stay secure in her buttoned pocket during the landing. She put it back around her neck and blew bird calls from the shore. She didn't bother with pleasantries, occupying herself with calling out towards the ship on the horizon. Every few minutes, between securing the gliders and talking with the villagers, she'd go back to her bird calls, listening for replies from animals or other allies who knew her codes. Each whistle since they landed was the same. &quot;Here I am. Where are you?&quot; to anyone who knew her sounds. <br /> <br /> <b>On the Deck of the Guild Ship Blue Lily, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour after Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;They're really quite good,&quot; the cook grumbled. &quot;Especially with a good stuffing and cider...&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The bird narrowed it's eyes a little. &quot;Better men than you have tried...&quot; he grumbled, his tone suddenly much more intelligible. <br /> <br /> He fluffed his feathers and shifted along his perch just above the crew's heads as the Captain made to shoo him along. &quot;No please Captain? Fluffy has no manners.&quot; He reached over and grabbed one of the slip nots the crew had used to tie off bits of rigging, giving it a firm jerk. He fluttered over to a few other loose looking slip knots and gave them all his best yank, laughing at the sound of things coming undone on the ship. There was only so much damage one little bird could do in a few quick moments but it would stall them a bit. He took off, blowing a raspberry at the crew as he circled once more around the ship, pooping on the cook for good measure as he turned towards the shore. <br /> <br /> As he flew close to the shoreline he heard the familiar sound of Wahine's whistle. &quot;I'm here. Where are you?&quot; He repeated the whistle. &quot;I'm hear, where are you?&quot;<br /> <br /> Wahine repeated herself more frequently and he'd reply in turn, honing in on her location. Eventually as the cluster of village people became clear he circled around and landed on Wahine's outstretched hand, relenting to a brief cuddle. Wahine kissed her feathered friend on his scalloped, ashen head. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T00:57:28-07:00","id":285770,"title":"","content":"(Wow, way to throw me into the story.)<br /> <br /> The old man reached for his hip, quickly checking himself for injuries, and to soothe the pain of the fall. Luckily, it wasn't broken, just bruised. If he got out of this situation, it would definatly leave a mark. He grabbed his staff, which had rolled to the side and clutched it in his arm, but didn't get off the ground. He knew the sound of a knife being sharpened. If he made any sudden movements, or seemed threathening in any way to the knife-wielding stranger, it would mean death. Whoever the man, or spirit was, at the moment, he only saw Hasya as an old priest, and that was a good thing. In situations like these, you had to think positive.<br /> <br /> &quot;Please, spare me.&quot; The old assassin said, getting on his knees and bowing towards the sound of the man's voice, his forehead pressed against the soil. &quot;It is as you say, I'm an old priest, nothing more, what good would killing me do you?&quot; He asked, but honestly, he didn't really want an answer. With his staff still in his hands, Hasya slowly raised his head, finally trying to make eyecontact with the knife-wielding man, if it was a man at all. He knew he looked pathetic, but he'd rather be pathetic and alive than proud and dead. The man sounded arrogant, so maybe he could stall for time by inflating it's ego, until someone could come and help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","user":"While My Guitar","date":". 10-18-2014, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T07:06:49-07:00","id":290479,"title":"","content":"<b><i>OOC: In considering Language stuff, I've decided to implement a text-color rule going forward so we don't have to write &quot;he said in Old Realm&quot; or &quot;He said in Seatongue&quot; or what have you, given that a language barrier's coming up. From now on, default-black text is in the Barbarian Tongue of Whitestone Island.<span style=\"color:#008080\"> This turquoise blue color is Seatongue.</span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">This deep purplish color is Old Realm</span><span style=\"color:#800080\">.</span><span style=\"color:#800080\"> High Realm is lighter purple,</span><span style=\"color:#EE82EE\"> and Low Realm is pink.</span><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Firetongue, predictably, is red. </span><span style=\"color:#AFEEEE\">Airtongue is light blue. </span><span style=\"color:#008000\">Riverspeak is green, </span><span style=\"color:#FF8C00\">Guild Cant is orange. </span>Right now that's all the languages likely to come up, but I'll add others if and when people learn them. Please start using these text color rules so I know what languages you're speaking and what NPCs can and cannot understand you. I tried to pick darker colors for the three most common languages so the contrast with the forum's background will be easy on the eyes, but if any of these colors are painful for you to look at or impossible for you to read, let me know and we can change them. I'm not going to go back and edit old posts-this should only have an effect on the conversation the Maiden's been having aboard the Blue Lily. Assume most of that conversation has been in Old Realm (which the Captain and Menreiki speak), but since the sailors don't know it much of what they've been saying or the Captain has been saying to them has been in Seatongue.</i><br /> <br /> Calm Sea Village, RY 67, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> Haku pulled his glider gently from the surf and began folding it up into an awkward and unwieldy shape which was nevertheless compact enough to carry on one's back through the jungle.<br /> <br /> &quot;Damn,&quot; he muttered, looking at Seskan's wrecked glider the way you'd look at a puppy who had just been kicked. &quot;Slow on the turns, but she was a beauty...Seskan, you're going to fix that glider for your friend, or I swear to Keshet I'm going to beat the shit out of you. Take care fishing it out of the water, don't get sand stuck in the wings.&quot;<br /> <br /> As Wahine began calling her bird and Fokisi and Seskan began speaking, the leader of Chief Kalewa's elite Kitemen ignored them, putting away his glider with a smooth ease borne of years of repetition. He was drawing interested looks from the people of Calm Sea Village who were gathered on the beach: first because the Kitemen are famous for their daring and bravery, and second because Cloudhopper Haku was graced by the gods and by his own discipline with a fantastic body and rippling muscles which were a simple joy to watch in motion.<br /> <br /> &quot;Whoever they are,&quot; Haku declared as he finished packing away his glider, &quot;we have about half an hour before reinforcements arrive. I'm Haku, First Kiteman for Chief Kalewa, and I signalled for assistance. The Chief will know about that ship in short order, and more Kitemen will show up soon. If they do seem hostile, we should try to delay any action until they arrive. I've seen a couple of ships like this before, usually way out at sea, but once or twice they've come to shore and tried to kidnap our people, gods only know why. We have some experience sinking these vessels from above with jugs of oil and flaming arrows. I recommend we send a boat out to meet them and do our diplomacy at sea: if the talks go bad, they'll be much harder to defeat if we allow them to make shore.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Wahine, feel free to have your bird repeat whatever it heard when it gets back to the beach. The Maiden doesn't speak Seatongue, so you should assume her conversations with Menreiki or Captain Phi Ho are in Old Realm. Things Captain Phi Ho are saying to the crew, or things crew members are saying, are in Seatongue, so you can understand them. The priest who's on the beach does know some Old Realm, so he can translate, though haltingly. </i><br /> <br /> <b>On the Deck of the Guild Ship Blue Lily, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> OOC: In the interest of not having to type<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#4B0082\">&quot;Well,&quot;</span> Captain Phi Ho smiled. <span style=\"color:#4B0082\">&quot;If they're friendly, we have plenty of iron weapons in the hold. Those usually sell well this far West, islanders rarely have access to good iron and they have a need to be able to defend themselves from the Raksha. We also have some Firedust, and while I'm reluctant to sell it, it's always exciting to people who have never seen it before. Since we're here for a while, we'll need food and provisions, the men could use some fresh fruit and meat, and if I can get one of them to sell me one of those gliders I'll be a rich man as soon as we can get it home and figure out how it works. I'm not much of a slaver, but the Lily's brig is big enough to hold a couple of folks, and attractive young islanders sell pretty well back in the Realm if you play up how exotic they are...but that's if they offer first, you don't ask if people's kids are for sale unless they bring it up. A bit rude, you know. Anyway, the bulk of our trade is going to be iron tools and textiles for provisions, at least until we establish a rapport with the locals. The real money in this venture is in putting this place on the map...and in those gliders, if we can reproduce them.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He tugged one of his whiskers in thought.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Captain? The gliders have landed, and they're talking to the people on the beach.&quot; </span>The sailor in the crow's nest called down. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;There are three of them, two men and woman...I'm a pretty decent lipreader, and I can see 'em just fine with the telescope, but I have no idea what they're talking about.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;We have the Maiden, she was born here. Hopefully she can translate for us.&quot;</span> The captain shrugged. &quot;<span style=\"color:#4B0082\">We're sailors, and we have firedust cannon. Therefore, if they do turn out to be hostile, we want to keep the engagement out here on the sea-a good hit looks like it would obliterate any of the boats they've got, and a shelling from the sea could incinerate their village. I hope we don't go that way, but I'd like to keep the option. Maiden...I'm going to put you in a boat along with a couple of my men and send you out to meet them on the beach. We'll keep a telescope on you, if things turn hostile we'll give you a warning shot to intimidate them with the thunder, and if they really go south we can support you with cannon and send more men. I intend to stay here, my appearance tends to frighten people. Menreiki, I recommend you do the same, at least until the locals have gotten used to our presence here.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <b>In the Jungle About One Day's Hike from Dreaming River Village and About Half An Hour's Hike from the Tomb of the Stone Maw, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> Pakari made his way quickly through the jungle. It was a little eerie. The birds were still chirping and the frogs were still croaking high up in the trees like nothing was wrong...but all the little faces and crawling shapes and grumpy little decaying leaf-sprites he was so used to seeing about their business in the corner of his eye were...just gone. The forest, so full of life, felt so empty. He wondered if this was how most people saw the jungle all the time...<br /> <br /> For her part, the Bearer didn't notice much that was unusual as she followed Pakari. He was easy to track: he was big, and strong, not incredibly graceful, and in a hurry. Therefore, he was at the front of a trail of broken branches and bent underbrush and snapped vines.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: If the Bearer is trying to avoid Pakari's attention, or if she's otherwise trying to do the stealthy ninja-thing so's she can take people unawares, make a Dex+Stealth roll, please. Attempting to sneak at speed (avoiding Pakari's notice while still gaining on him or keeping up with him as he hurries without attempting stealth) will give you a one-point difficulty penalty to your roll.</i><br /> <br /> <b>At The Tomb of the Stone Maw, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> As he raised his head, Hasya saw something move within the shadows of the great stone mouth. Something big. Then the knife-scraping sound again...as he peered forward, he saw several sparks leap to life as razor-edged stone caught on stone, briefly illuminating the source of the voice.<br /> <br /> It was sharpening its claws on the stone walls of the passageway. They were maybe eight inches long, its claws, and curved...it was huge, and it was looking down at him and smiling with teeth like steak knives, and its skin was smooth and black like wet obsidian, and it crouched on four huge legs and its eyes were gleaming orbs the color of the sea at moonrise...the spark died, and again he could see only a shadow within the great stone maw.<br /> <br /> &quot;I love killing priests,&quot; the voice purred. &quot;I wouldn't gain much, but I'm probably still going to eat you, just as a matter of principle. Slowly. It's been so very long since I tasted blood, you see, and so I intend to savor it...tell me, old priest, what good would sparing you do me?&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Int+Occult to recognize what you're dealing with based on a brief glimpse of the creature. </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 10-23-2014, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T05:41:38-08:00","id":307341,"title":"","content":"The Maiden frowned, as if she is a child who has just been denied her treat, &quot;<span style=\"color:#4B0082\">Puh, such nonsense, nobody can resist a handsome and fluffy kitty such as you !&quot;, </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">she then unexpectedly reached out toward the Captain, &quot;Wait Maiden, what are yo.....urg&quot;, </span>the tigerman didn't have time to react as the raven-haired girl tried to pull both his cheeks into a big smile, &quot;<span style=\"color:#4B0082\">All you need to do is SMIL...............EEEEhhhhhh.......&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">.<br /> <br /> The Captain is just....pure scary when up-close,</span> now that the Maiden thought about it, she have never stand close to captain Phi Ho, isn't she ? Kinda make the girl wonder why her master can invade the captain's personal space so.........nonchalantly, well, he's invade everyone's personal space, but she thought he would at least keep some distance with the Captain, isn't tiger eat rabbit in the wild....?<br /> <br /> A long awkward moment pass through the Blue Lily ship as everyone is wide-eyed at the normally ladylike Maiden who just did something to the Captain that none of the crew dare to, &quot;<span style=\"color:#4B0082\">.......I will do as you said, Captain.....Oh hey, the magic spy bird just left.&quot;,</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> after realizing that everyone was staring at her, the Maiden tried to deflect the attention</span> toward the strange bird but then she remembered that only her master and the Captain can understand her.....Ooooh, she should have listened to her master at learning Seatongue after all, thought the Maiden as she tried to hide her cheeks that were blushing furiously.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T11:51:33-08:00","id":308411,"title":"","content":"Pakari ran as fast as he could without tripping over anything. He wove through the trees, following water trails, streambeds, animal tracks, and other places where the footing was comparatively clear. Islanders didn't travel through this part of the island much, except to hunt or forage, which unfortunately meant that Pakari would have to bushwhack the whole way to and from the Tomb of the Stone Maw. Normally that was a non-issue, but just now time was of the essence, and Pakari cursed the lack of a proper trail at least once every thirty steps.<br /> <br /> The forest felt deserted with no spirits around. The space felt desolate without them. Had Pakari been less focused on running, the eeriness of the depopulated forest would have been overwhelming.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Pakari had been able to see the spirits for most of his life. He dimly remembered trying to play with them when he could barely walk or talk, and being disappointed that he could not touch them. It took several years for him to realize that other people could not see what he saw, and that some thought him touched in the head or just stupid because he would talk to &quot;imaginary friends&quot; or spend long periods of time staring into &quot;empty&quot; spaces. For a long time, only Aroha understood his gift, and she only knew because she had the presence of mind to talk to the priests when Pakari refused to admit that the strange animals and faces he saw in the trees were not real.<br /> <br /> By his early teens, he had gotten practiced at the art of pretending to be normal, which mostly meant not watching the spirits when there were other people around. Ignoring them was not always easy - spirits were sensitive to many things that people were not, and if something startled them (such as the earthquake today), Pakari was always the first to notice and react, which could be awkward when Pakari was among company. Still, despite the occasional hiccup, Pakari managed to do a reasonably good job of integrating into the Dreaming River community without getting a reputation for being insane or delusional. Still, he felt that the difference between his experience of the world and those of others put a gap between him and almost everyone else he knew.<br /> <br /> Confessing to Hasya that he could see things no one else could had been one of the most cathartic experiences of his life, and the old priest had been surprisingly (from Pakari's point of view) understanding and supportive.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> (Rolling Perception+Awareness to detect the Bearer - 9,7,5,5,1. 2 Successes)<br /> <br /> Still, the lack of distractions might have worked in Pakari's favor. When he made a quick turn around a tree, he spotted something out of the corner of his eye to the south. He did a double-take and stopped running for just a moment to see a large woman with a sword and a ragged cloak coming through the brush behind him. He blinked a few times, completely confused about why the Bearer was there, and called back to her. &quot;Hey. Hey! Are you following me? What do you want?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 11-11-2014, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T02:20:12-08:00","id":308906,"title":"","content":"<i>OOC: Normally, Semicasual, I'd wait on the results of the Bearer's stealth roll before letting you spot and talk to her...but, well, you two just running in silence towards a place some distance away is boring for both of you, and you're likely gonna be waiting on While My Guitar's conversation with the creature that appears to want to eat him, so it's best if you have each other to talk to.</i><br /> <br /> <b>On the Deck of the Guild Ship Blue Lily, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> There was a long, quiet pause as the crew stared at the Maiden and the Captain in shock.<br /> <br /> Then Captain Phi Ho burst into a deep, rolling laugh, and everyone breathed a sigh of relief. Everyone except Menreiki, whose ears stood straight up and whose lip was pursed in obvious irritation.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#4B0082\">&quot;Well what are we waiting for,&quot; </span>Menreiki declared grumpily.<span style=\"color:#4B0082\"> &quot;Let's get on with it! But there's no way I am sending my protege out into danger alone, Captain! Unlike yourself, I am able to avail myself in such situations of that most fashionable and practical of inventions, the hat.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Menreiki proceeded to pull a small fur cap from nowhere (the man was, after all, an accomplished master of the stage, and sleight of hand came easily to him) and gingerly folded his ears to place it snugly upon his head. He still looked very grumpy about something, and for some reason Menreiki looking grumpy just made the Captain smile wider and chuckle more deeply.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Aye, you're right. Get to the boats! Let's see...Lefty, Red Smile, Distant Thunder, and...Vorapu. You four go with them. Menreiki's in charge, Maiden will translate for him...and Menreiki? If things go south, Red Smile's the boss, got it?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Aye, Captain,&quot;</span> Menreiki declared, eyeing Red Smile warily. There wasn't really another way to eye Red Smile: the man was half again as tall as Menreiki was, with arms like well-muscled tree trunks and deep bronze skin covered in swirling tattoos depicting a dragon wrestling a tentacled sea monster, and a rather unusual number of scars. The huge warrior grinned (his teeth were not, in fact, red, but rather a gleaming white) and showed them to the rowboats. The Captain could no doubt have fit three more men on the rowboat with them if Red Smile had stayed on the ship...but no doubt he knew what he was doing.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Let us be off, then!&quot;</span> Menreiki cried, seized with the sense of the dramatic as he sat in the rowboat.<span style=\"color:#4B0082\"> &quot;Whooah!&quot;</span> He cried, as the rowboat fell out from under him to the sea below with a sudden lurch.<br /> <br /> And then they were on the open water, the ship behind them, the burly eye-patch wearing Lefty and tall lean and quiet Distant Thunder rowing while the pale Northerner Vorapu loaded several firewands, just in case. Red Smile watched the beach through a small telescope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 11-24-2014, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T08:41:21-08:00","id":313742,"title":"","content":"The Maiden gazed at her master with the usual nonchalantly look and bowed before captain Phi Ho before descend down onto the boat with a tattooed bronze giant and an over enthusiastic rabbit man.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800080\">Aw kiddo, what with that over serious look. If you succeed then we can stay at the island and enjoy the beach, if you fail then the local hate us and chase us around the beach. It'll be fun either way, so cheer up&quot;</span>, Merenki was looking at the island when he noticed the Maiden overserious expression and try to give her the usual pep talk.<br /> <br /> Damn master, it's very hard to remain grumpy when you talk like that in front of an endless blue sky as the ocean's song ringing in the background. <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;I...idiot master, it's not that I worry about disappointing you and the Captain or anything</span>&quot;, when Merenki heard the Maiden said those words he immediately made a........very strange face, his eyes was wide open like someone just told him a very unfunny joke or something.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800080\">Uuuhh Master, what wrong with what I just said ?</span>&quot;, the Maiden certainly thought the phrase was perfect for that moment, she always want to said something like that after reading &quot;The Golden Harem&quot;, one of the character said those exact words when she save the protagonist from the evil Ma-ha-sushi, she even make a cool entrance by throwing a single white flower on the lake where the final battle between her and the antagonist took place, the Maiden even keep one dried flower in her sleeve so she can toss it into the ocean after she said that, she thought it will be so evocative and poetic, but seeing her master's expression, maybe......she will do it in another time.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/2JBJTjY.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 12-17-2014, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T00:06:56-08:00","id":320527,"title":"","content":"The old priest didn't reply, still kneeling in front of the creature, he wanted to seem defenseless, weak, maybe even cowardly. It wouldn't make the creature see pity, but at the very least the creature wouldn't see him as a threat.<br /> &quot;I...&quot; He began, quickly realizing that what he would say would just waste time, and quickly closing his mouth again.<br /> &quot;I understand.&quot; He said, looking up at the creature. &quot;Before you kill me, can you at least tell me your name?<br /> Based on the creature's behaviour, Hasya concluded that it was an arrogant and cruel creature, and based on the claws, it had to be quite dangerous, but had to come close to actually injure him, if he knew the weak spot on this creature, a quick stab with his knife should be enough. It was only a ritual knife, used to sacrifice animals, but it was still very sharp.<br /> <br /> (Roll Int+Occ result:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://dice.brainclouds.net/Result.aspx?ID=4WDGX42M\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://dice.brainclouds.net/Result.aspx?ID=4WDGX42M\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://dice.brainclouds.net/Result.aspx?ID=4WDGX42M\" target=\"_blank\"> http://dice.brainclouds.net/Result.aspx?ID=4WDGX42M </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div> <br /> 2, 2, 9, 10, 10, 10, for a total of 7 successes. This is the first time I get more successes than die I rolled.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T13:31:07-08:00","id":321029,"title":"","content":"<i>OOC: Nice roll! I was gonna tell you the species of the creature on a three, so I'll give you four extra pieces of information which Hasya may find useful in dealing with it.</i><br /> <br /> <b>At The Tomb of the Stone Maw, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> The brief glimpse of the creature was enough to tell Hasya a great deal. This beast was a demon, a great regal cat of living black jade. It was one of the Teodozjia, an unholy race of demons who share one great and ancient mind between them, who hate the gods above all else, and who love nothing more than profaning sacred places or symbols and tormenting priests until they lost their faith.<br /> <br /> This one seemed a bit bigger than usual, but maybe that was fear talking.<br /> <br /> Now that Hasya was thinking about the Teodozjia, every story he could think of involving them (and there were only a couple of stories, mostly involving a priest who grows corrupt and then goes mad summoning the things in profane ceremonies before some ancient chieftain and his warriors put it down with heavy losses), these demons spoke in the plural. It was always, &quot;we are displeased with you, foolish mortal&quot; or &quot;We will punish the servants of the gods&quot;...this one was using Me and I. Had the wards cut it off from the shared mind of its kin? Surely for a creature like this, such loneliness would be almost intolerable!<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;You are surprisingly brave.&quot; The monster's purr echoed forth from the Stone Maw. &quot;Most would at least try to flee the inevitable...I can respect that bravery, priest. I was bound here by my name, long ago, and only a provincial Moon-Chosen's ignorance of my full title left me the freedom to hunt during the nights when the Moon hides her accursed face. I am therefore loathe to give you my name...but your courage in the face of your end deserves to be honored.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hearing its voice, reflecting on the stories, knowing what it was...Hasya came to some rapid conclusions. First, the creature was cut off from its kin, and therefore probably near madness from isolation, which explained why it was talking to him. Second, if an imperfect binding had allowed it to roam free during the New Moon, then there were two sets of wards here: the original imperfect binding set when the Tomb was built, and the additional wards placed by the ancient High Priest in the story to seal it back in again after its rampages. If the wards destroyed during the storm were what had held it in the Tomb during the New Moon...then it was still bound, at least until nightfall six days hence. Therefore, the damned thing was bluffing about eating him, and Hasya was actually perfectly safe. In fact, demons being what they were, centuries of boredom and maddening loneliness were probably only part of why it was bothering to talk to him. It was also probably hatching some clever scheme to try and trick him into letting it loose before the New Moon.<br /> <br /> &quot;Give up your loyalty to your treacherous gods. Swear to serve me for the rest of your days, priest, and I shall spare you and any you can persuade to follow you in my service.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ah, yes. There it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 12-17-2014, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T23:20:41-08:00","id":334867,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">B] Calm Sea Village, RY 67, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise: [/B]<br /> </span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/239065-ic-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign?p=284249#post284249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">&quot;We do not know. From what we saw, the ship isn't like the ones who usually trade in here. Perhaps they are simply merchants or travelers, and maybe they are something more. the dear lady&quot; he said, while turning to the silent woman &quot;in her wisdom, has sent her talking bird as a spy- and when it would return we may discover a thing or two about those who live in the ship&quot;</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> [FONT=Helvetica]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru;n290479[/FONT</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Haku pulled his glider gently from the surf and began folding it up into an awkward and unwieldy shape which was nevertheless compact enough to carry on one's back through the jungle.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">&quot;Damn,&quot; he muttered, looking at Seskan's wrecked glider the way you'd look at a puppy who had just been kicked. &quot;Slow on the turns, but she was a beauty...Seskan, you're going to fix that glider for your friend, or I swear to Keshet I'm going to beat the shit out of you. Take care fishing it out of the water, don't get sand stuck in the wings.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">As Wahine began calling her bird and Fokisi and Seskan began speaking, the leader of Chief Kalewa's elite Kitemen ignored them, putting away his glider with a smooth ease borne of years of repetition. He was drawing interested looks from the people of Calm Sea Village who were gathered on the beach: first because the Kitemen are famous for their daring and bravery, and second because Cloudhopper Haku was graced by the gods and by his own discipline with a fantastic body and rippling muscles which were a simple joy to watch in motion.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">&quot;Whoever they are,&quot; Haku declared as he finished packing away his glider, &quot;we have about half an hour before reinforcements arrive. I'm Haku, First Kiteman for Chief Kalewa, and I signalled for assistance. The Chief will know about that ship in short order, and more Kitemen will show up soon. If they do seem hostile, we should try to delay any action until they arrive. I've seen a couple of ships like this before, usually way out at sea, but once or twice they've come to shore and tried to kidnap our people, gods only know why. We have some experience sinking these vessels from above with jugs of oil and flaming arrows. I recommend we send a boat out to meet them and do our diplomacy at sea: if the talks go bad, they'll be much harder to defeat if we allow them to make shore.&quot;</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Wahine grit her teeth at being addressed as 'dear lady\u2019. She did have a name, if only people thought to ask. She found such empty politeness irritating, especially from someone she\u2019d only just met. As someone who communicated largely through body language, her flash of annoyance was easy to see. She pushed her way through the thickening crowd of onlookers who seemed hopelessly in her way. If she had her staff she\u2019d rap them in the ankles to force them out of her way. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">\u201cGive way, give way!\u201d her bird shouted as he fluttered to the ground and toddled through the cluster of feet around Foksi and Seskan. He began twittering away random snatches of conversation in a variety of languages and voices. Wahine thought she heard the occasional snatch of sea tongue but the rest was foreign to her. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Her irritated expression softened when she approached Haku making short work of binding the glider into a portable bundle. She loosened the bundle enough to reach her hand inside and pluck out the staff which she had fastened to one of the braces. She smiled sweetly at Haku, placing a reassuring hand on his arm as she followed drifting gaze to the pieces of Seskan's damaged glider. She brushed a lock of hair from his face and looked him in the eyes. <br /> <br /> <i> Don't worry, I can fix it. </i> her eyes said. The moment of wordless intimacy lasted only a lingering second and the she quickly moved onto something else. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Among her possessions she\u2019d fished out of the water was her small little shoulder bag. It didn\u2019t hold much and she hadn\u2019t brought much with her, just the essentials; rudimentary pocket tools for an emergency, a pretty basic spyglass for sightseeing, and a small utility knife. The spyglass was small and basic but she reckoned she could make some field adjustments to improve the range a little. Unable to communicate clearly, she just didn\u2019t bother with typical the social graces and was too focused on her spyglass to notice reactions as she combed through the crowd looking for materials she could use. It took a few minutes but quick as lightening she was able to make some field tweaks to the pretty basic device. She could make out the approaching landing party much clearer now. She handed the spyglass to Haku wordlessly and pointed towards the ship.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">(rolled a 9-8-10-10-3-4-6-7 on a craft roll if needed to do a field modification of a small, basic spyglass.)</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T22:26:33-08:00","id":336778,"title":"","content":"<b>Calm Sea Village, RY 67, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Thank you, Wahine.&quot; Haku took the spyglass with a wry smile and looked out to see. &quot;Looks like they're sending a boat ashore...I see a couple of warriors including a huge man with many scars, who I take to be their leader. There are two others, though...a thin little man with a strange hat. He must be a priest...and there's a woman.&quot;<br /> <br /> Haku raised his eyebrow. &quot;The others are obviously foreigners, by their eyes and by their dress and by the shape of their faces, but...this woman is of our people, though she wears strange clothing. The others do not speak to her, except for the priest, and the two make faces at each other like old lovers. I...am not really sure what to make of this. It's obviously not a raiding party. Should we take a boat out and meet them at sea, or let them land on the beach?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T09:15:28-08:00","id":338096,"title":"","content":"Wahine looked out at the sea with an expression of deep thought on her face. She grabbed a stray twig and began scratching a picture in the ground. She drew the shore, people on the beach, a small boat right at the tideline just before a the point where people would disembark into the water to pull the boat securely up to shore above the tideline. She scratched the words 'strong, stable ground, advantage' above the shore people and scratched the words 'weak, no stable ground, moving, limited attack room, busy with boat&quot;. She looked up from her drawing to see if Haku was watching, tapping him gently on the ankle as she crouched and pointing marking a point in her picture with an X. Her message she was trying to get across was 'they will be weakest when they are trying to bring their boat up to shore. They will have their hands full with the boat and will have the ocean to wade through. We will be strongest on land while they are wading through the shallows and pulling their landing craft out of the sea.&quot; How much of that got through to him was anyone's guess. Well, at the very least maybe her picture would be useful. <br /> <br /> (rolled Charisma+socialise +1 die bonus for unspoken communication. 4,5,5,9: 1 success)<br /> (rolled Dex+craft (air) to draw a useful picture/diagram. - 2,5,5, 10,9,8 7,8: 6 successes)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T00:41:45-08:00","id":338812,"title":"","content":"Hasya quickly analyzed what he knew of the creature. These demons had an instinctual hatred of priests and other religious figures, if the lion could kill him, it would have. For at least a little while, he would be safe from the creature.<br /> &quot;Me? Serving a monster like you? I'd rather die.&quot; Hasya said, looking at the creature, not afraid anymore, there was nothing for him to be afraid of after all.<br /> Slowly, the old man stood back up, grabbing his staff and leaning on it to support himself. He prayed that he was right, because this could cost him his life.<br /> &quot;I may be old, and I may be weak, but I am still a priest, and before that, a member of the Green Flower tribe, and before that, a warrior, and I still have my pride. So, hellspawned beast, if you truely enjoy killing priests, and have not tasted blood as long as you claim. Then let me be your first meal, but I will not be your slave.&quot;<br /> For the first time, the priest did something to defy the creature. He took a step towards it, clutching his staff in one hand. He was afraid, sure, but his voice was calm. If the creature could eat him, it would, so the only thing he could do was watch. In the mean time, he looked over the creature, trying to see if there were any weaknesses he could exploit.<br /> <br /> (Roll, Perception+Occult to scan the lion for weaknesses, physical or otherwise, 2,5,8,9, so 2 successes)<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://dice.brainclouds.net/Result.aspx?ID=VEDEX7V6\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://dice.brainclouds.net/Result.aspx?ID=VEDEX7V6\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://dice.brainclouds.net/Result.aspx?ID=VEDEX7V6\" target=\"_blank\"> http://dice.brainclouds.net/Result.aspx?ID=VEDEX7V6 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T05:54:42-08:00","id":342842,"title":"","content":"<b>At The Tomb of the Stone Maw, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> &quot;A monster?&quot; The demon purred, again rattling the nearby stones. &quot;In all the centuries since the Kite Flute called me forth from nothingness, I have slain perhaps a hundred, maybe two hundred mortals...and most of these because I was bound to do so against my will, after the tomb I was forced to guard was robbed. If you are of the Green Flower Tribe, you no doubt revere Keshet, whose storms have surely killed many more. A man your age no doubt has friends or family who have been lost at sea in one of the Sun-Swallower's rampages, and you call me a monster? You continue to amuse, little priest, and your bravery continues to impress me...but are you not already a slave? What makes service to myself so much more onerous to you than service to the black serpent who feasts on blood and war, or Fintan, whose mudslides obliterate whole villages when she is displeased?&quot;<br /> <br /> The beast lay down in the entrance to the stone maw, bringing its huge dark eyes level with Hasya's.<br /> <br /> &quot;Would you speak to them as you speak to me, were they bound as I am?&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Calm Sea Village, RY 67, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> &quot;What are you..?&quot; Haku looked down at Wahine's picture in the sand, then smiled. &quot;You know, if you weren't already such a shipwright, you might have made a fine warrior. If I were going to attack them, I'd do it as you suggest...but it's a poor way to have a conversation, making the other guy stand up to his waist in the surf and manhandle a boat while he's trying to talk to you...But you're right, it's best to let them come ashore. We have the advantage of numbers here, but if we take a boat out to meet them we lose it, and they're close to their reinforcements. Also, waiting for them to arrive gives my gliders more time to spread my message and show up to help out if we need them.&quot;<br /> <br /> He crossed his arms and looked out to see again, spyglass to his eye. &quot;If it comes down to it, I'll take the big one with the scars.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Aboard the Guild Ship <i>Blue Lily's </i>rowboat, the <i>Petal</i>, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> Menreiki smiled at her delivery. <span style=\"color:#4B0082\">&quot;I love that one. I don't know if we've got the talent for The Golden Harem, anytime soon though, kiddo. I mean, you could pull off the role, and I could play the hero, but you need somebody real big with a nice deep voice for the villain on that one. The Captain'd make a good Ma Ha Suchi, now I think of it...but I'm not sure what his singing voice is like.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Red Smile put down his telescope. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;There are about thirty of them. Warriors waiting up by the treeline, assorted villagers scattered through the area...they don't know what to make of us. Big man out front watching us with a spyglass, and it looks like everyone is doing what he says or doing what the other man up the beach says. If it comes to a fight, I'll take the man with the spyglass. Vorapu, you stay with me, let loose with the firewands. The noise and the flame should startle them enough to keep their distance while we fall back to the boat. Distant Thunder, Lefty, you're on bodyguard duty. Don't let anything happen to the Captain's pet rabbit.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Aye, sir.&quot;</span> Lefty grinned.<br /> <br /> Menreiki frowned.<span style=\"color:#4B0082\"> &quot;Pet rabbit indeed,&quot;</span> he muttered.<span style=\"color:#4B0082\">&quot;This pet rabbit could buy and sell you ten times over...&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;What was that?&quot;</span> Red Smile asked.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;I, um. I was telling the Maiden to stay near behind you and Vorapu. In case we need to run for the boat.&quot;</span> Menreiki gave the huge man a big smile. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Just in case. </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">Hey, kid. If things go bad, stay between the big guys and the boat. They'll make a big explosion to startle the locals while we make a run for it. And if we get captured, make big eyes at whatever warrior's in charge and try to seduce 'em into not eating me or anything, okay?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The boat slid into the shallows. From here they could see the faces of the men and women on shore. The Maiden could even hear their voices, talking to each other in a familiar language...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Can she understand what they're saying?&quot;</span> Lefty asked.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#4B0082\">&quot;Can you understand them? Yell that we're just here to talk, and to trade, maybe?&quot;</span> Menreiki stage-whispered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 12-17-2014, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T22:27:31-08:00","id":343693,"title":"","content":"Wahine actually smirked wryly at Haku's comment before a far more common roll of the eyes. She appreciated the praise but had no reason to think his understanding of her had gained any new depth recently. As far as she knew, none of her suitors had ever bothered pick up any sign language and she had better things to do then write long, eloquent answers to questions people never cared to ask. She picked up her staff and quickly trotted down towards the water's edge, stopping about a meter from where the largest of the morning's waves lapped against the damp sand of the receding tide. She held her hands open to show she meant no harm and carried no weapon besides her staff. She looked up the beach and at the tree line where people seemed to be clustering and held a hand out to signal everyone behind her to wait and stand down. It was gutsy, putting herself suddenly between anyone who may be hiding just within the tree line, the villagers who where quite capable of taking up arms themselves if threatened, and the potentially hostile visitors. While the rest of the villagers decided what to do, at least the presence of a woman would be was less intimidating than men with all the marks and bearings of a warrior class. She didn't think they where looking at a fight. If the visitors where purely hostile and only interested in ransacking the place, then why not shower the whole place with cannon fire first? No... there had to be more to it than that. All she could hope was that her signal was taken as a non-confrontational one as their craft floated through the shallows and she could hear the sounds of languages both strange and familiar. <br /> <br /> For a tense moment, she waited. Arms open, she hoped they'd stay their weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T07:14:08-08:00","id":351624,"title":"","content":"Kia, it's the important moment where the Maiden have to speak to the islander (from afar of course, but still...). Most of the time it is always her Master who handle this kind of thing, now that the spotlight has moved onto the Maiden she is starting to have sweating hands and increased heart-rated, is this the legendary &quot;Rookie Surprise&quot; the her Master used to mention, the Maiden covered her mouth in horror, not realizing everyone puzzled look toward her.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#4B0082\">&quot;Arrggh, I will just have to do my best, mysterious islander, here I come !&quot;</span>, there is no time for pondering, since she don't want to get her head chew off by the Captain after all.<br /> <br /> The Maiden pulled from her long, wide and poofy sleeve a bronze blowhorn that her Master purchased from a Southern bazaard, even though the merchant said that it's a musical instrument, but the sound is so loud that his ears almost explode when he tried to use it the first time, too bad that merchant's stand has already disappeared when an angry bunny man came looking for retribution.<br /> <br /> Menrenki realized the thing in the Maiden's hands and immediately told everyone to cover their ears.<br /> <br /> The Maiden took a long breath before unleashing her charismatic voice, &quot;WE HAVE COME IN PEACE, IF IT IS NOT TOO MUCH TROUBLE, WOULD YOU BE SO KIND AS TO ALLOW OUR SHIPS TO LAND ON YOUR SHORE !&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T23:30:01-08:00","id":357289,"title":"","content":"Though usually stoic and firm in the face of the unknown, such a great noise emanating so suddenly not much beyond a few boat lengths out to sea from such a small figure was enough to make Wahine jump like a cat thrown into a boiling pot. The fact that the noise was in the local language was an afterthought.<br /> <br /> <i>Great, now I'm mute AND deaf.</i><br /> <br /> She marked an X in the sand for them to aim for and waved them towards her with a free hand as she tried to stop the ringing in her ears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T19:38:24-08:00","id":361950,"title":"","content":"<br /> <b>Calm Sea Village, RY 67, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> As the boat pulled up to shore and the Maiden bellowed through her bullhorn, the men and women along the shore winced and covered their ears.<br /> <br /> &quot;You can land your boat,&quot; Haku yelled back. &quot;So that we can talk! But the ship stays out in the bay until we know who you are and what you want!&quot;<br /> <br /> The boat slid to shore, and the burly men within hopped out and pulled it up onto the sand, jostling the boat in the process so that Menreiki, who had been standing up, promptly fell over.<br /> <br /> &quot;Who are you?&quot; Haku asked as the boat arrived. Wahine noticed that he couldn't help looking upon the strangely dressed woman with admiration- Haku was many things, but subtle he was not, and he was destined never to win any gambling game based upon bluffing the opponent.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T09:21:57-08:00","id":365471,"title":"","content":"As the Maiden saw master who has just face-planted himself onto the sand, &quot;<span style=\"color:#4B0082\">Aye</span>&quot;, she sighed and grabbing Menrenki's arm to tried and help him get up.......Wait, one of the Captain's crewmate is being interrogate by a burly and rugged man !<br /> <br /> She immediately let go of Menreiki and rushed toward Thunder and Haku &quot;<span style=\"color:#4B0082\">Do not worry sir, I'm here to help !</span>&quot;, this is it, here come the Raven-Haired Maiden's big moment, her charismatic spee..&quot;<span style=\"color:#4B0082\">Kiiii !!!!</span>&quot;. The moment her okobo touched the sand it instantly sunk into the ground, and thus all those momentum that suppose to make her great entrance are now helping her fly toward the crowd.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ylozq5j.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 01-10-2015, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T22:55:56-08:00","id":368309,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Without thinking Wahine rushed to catch the girl as she toppled forward, just barely managing to catch her in her arms before she hit the sand. (one success Dex+Athletics). Wahine was surprisingly strong for a woman of her stature; grip firm and calloused from years hammering and carving the raw materials of the world into elegant and useful forms. She was a few inches taller than the average daughter of Whitestone and had a longer and leaner look than many a buxom island girl. But beneath her simple shorts and tunic, she had a healthy curvaceous figure far removed from the half-starved years of her youth. A few strands of hair poked out from a simple, wind-picked braid that hung to the middle of her back. At first glance her hair appeared dark as squid ink but in the sunlight it had a faint blueish sheen. Though dressed down and in need of a little grooming, Wahine was an attractive woman in a wholesome, natural sort of way. <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">She did have one distinguished article on her though; a necklace of durable woven twine that held a pendent of cold iron framed on each side by several beads of the island's attractive white stone.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>It\u2019s alright. </i>She said with only her eyes and a reassuring smile. She had a kind, pleasant face when she smiled and her eyes were the color of brilliant amethyst. She set the girl down at the point where the sand was less deep and packed more firmly, sparing a quick last minute inspection. Though it was brief, she looked her over as if she where inspecting a piece of fine art for nearly imperceptible blemishes. Satisfied, her steely gaze softened once more and she smiled one last time before trotting back to where she\u2019d dropped her staff a short moment ago. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">There was a rustle of feathers and the stout grey bird fluttered down to the sand where all the commotion seemed to be gathering. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">\u201cHi!\u201d he said to the maiden before catching sight of Wahine, toddling over to her, and stepping onto her outstretched hand. She smiled at her friend and began making a series of odd gestures in the air in front of the creature. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>Just in time, I might need you in a minute.</i></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","user":"Foxsimile","date":". 01-13-2015, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T01:10:25-08:00","id":368405,"title":"","content":"<br /> <b>Calm Sea Village, RY 67, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> The people on the beach were visibly relaxing. There was something decidedly nonthreatening about Menreiki and the Maiden, and even if the other men from the rowboat looked dangerous their obvious concern for the Maiden when she tripped and their obvious amusement at Menreiki's loss of balance made them seem much less threatening.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Looks like you've made a friend,&quot;</span> Red Smile chuckled. <span style=\"color:#008080\">&quot;Let's get to the negotiations. Tell them we're here to trade, and we mean no harm. We've just finished a long sea voyage and we are tired and hungry and happy to have found such a pleasant island. We hope that we will be able to be friends. Don't mention the cannons or anything threatening unless they get aggressive, no reason to frighten anyone unless we have to.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 01-13-2015, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T16:08:50-08:00","id":369109,"title":"","content":"Wahine made a mental note of the cannons and decided to keep her knowledge of sea tongue under wraps.<br /> <br /> <i>Don't let on that I know </i><i>sea tongue. </i>She signed in the local language on the off chance that one of the visitors recognized a gesture common to sea tongue. She doubted that any of them had any fluency in the dominant western sign language, much less a remote island tongue. Her bird watched her fingers flail about wildly, cocking his head to the side and betraying no other hint besides a bob of his head that he had picked up anything intelligible from her cluster of movements.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hungry!&quot; He whined, more out of self interest and an animal's attention span than a thoughtful attempt obscure any seriousness hidden in his mistress's messages. &quot;Brunch Brunch, Haku promised lunch... &quot; he sang at the group of men. Wahine handed him a nut from her pocket and he was momentarily satisfied with cracking open the hard-shelled morsel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","user":"Foxsimile","date":". 01-13-2015, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T12:28:43-08:00","id":378269,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/I6PRtif.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;.....so cool...~&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Stars began to sparkles in the Maiden's eyes as she gazed at the woman who just saved her only to be interrupted by her master who pounded at her from behind. The rabbit-ears man paraphrased Red Smile's intruction while meowing like a devious cat. The girl was about to lectured Merenki before he pushed her toward the crowd with a big grin on his face.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ohh, may Venus blessed me&quot;, Raven-haired whispered a small prayer toward the Sapphire Lady, she walked toward the crowd , her eyes glinted like a dark-night again the clear blue sky.<br /> <br /> &quot;Good morning everyone&quot;, the Maiden gathered everyone attention with a gentle greeting, &quot;Our apologize for causing such a commotion like this, but us merchants from faraway land mean no harm&quot;, her voice echoed softly through the beach, &quot;After crossing the ocean to arrive here, we hope that some of our merchandises will be of interested for the people of this paradise.&quot;, she continue her discourse while glancing and tenderly at the islander, sometime making small eyes contact with a person in the crowd to make everyone feel involved, &quot;But the crew are exhausted after such a long journey, and thus, I seek your approval for us to dock our ship and allow us to take rest.&quot;, the Maiden then bowed before the local people as a gesture of respect and courtesy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T01:26:38-08:00","id":404243,"title":"","content":"Wahine looked out her spy glass at the magnificent ship out at sea, studying and admiring it as only a master craftsman could. Her thoughts ran as the maiden spoke behind her. Though her back was turned, she listened intently, making shrewd mental calculations. No doubt a ship like that had a maintenance list a mile long. She should get back to the village and fire up her master's workshop. The semi-retired old bat would definitely want to get a jump on milling some fresh timber. The thought of trade excited her and she knew her carpentry skills alone gave her tremendous bargaining power. Her eyes glittered at the thought of what might be inside that massive hull. She made a mental note to introduce herself to the captain when she had a moment. Cozying up to the captain always had its advantages. But there would be time during the next few weeks as the crew restocked supplies, bartered their wares, and indulged in a little rest from the sea. At the moment, there was work to do and she wanted to get back her village. <br /> <br /> She collapsed her spyglass, marched over to Haku, and gave him a tap with her staff to get his attention as he communicated with the visitors.<br /> <br /> <i>I'm going back</i> she mouthed while signing. <i> I have work </i><br /> &quot;Return to village&quot; her parrot translated as he watched her fingers. &quot;Back to work&quot;<br /> <br /> Now to catch a ride up the river. By now surely reinforcements would be showing up. If there was a launch point nearby, the fast way home would be catching a ride on a glider, but she kept her eyes peeled for a river boat that might be heading up river. As soon as she sees a way back to the village, she'll head to her master's shop and get to work making trinkets and other products.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T08:11:55-08:00","id":421768,"title":"","content":"<b>Calm Sea Village, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> As Wahine headed towards the river in the hopes of catching a boat, her parrot abruptly fluffed its feathers and doubled in apparent size, squawked wordlessly, and took to the air. As she turned to watch its path, she could see inland through the break in the trees made by the winding of the river. In the inland forests, the trees were beginning to sway as though in a heavy wind...<br /> <br /> The Maiden was adorable and friendly, and the crowd was warming to her quickly. They were nodding and the locals were warming to the idea of letting the strangers dock their ship and rest...until the Maiden fell over again. This time she did not get up, and lay facedown in the sand twitching. Her clumsy friend from the boat rushed to her side and turned her over, and the people of Calm Sea Village started back in fear, for her eyes were wide and white and she muttered in a strange language.<br /> <br /> Haku was angrily demanding to know what was happening from the foreigners who couldn't understand his language, who were bristling defensively around the girl, when suddenly the beach bucked underneath them like a rolling wave. Seskan was caught off guard and lost his footing as the sand under him suddenly began pouring into a chasm, and he was almost drawn into it before a blast of hot wind from under the earth bodily lifted him and his damaged glider out of harm's way. He slammed into something heavy, and everything went fuzzy. Wahine had spent time at sea, and she had a few seconds of warning, so she kept her feet long enough to see the huts and villages of Calm Sea Village collapsing, trees being uprooted, cracks opening in the earth and black smoke pouring forth, to feel a wind like the air coming off a furnace blowing from somewhere inland and to hear an all-encompassing roar like that of a hurricane before a falling tree pinned her in place and broke several of her ribs.<br /> <br /> The watchtowers guarding the coastline from monsters of the southern sea swayed and fell. The Guild ship out at sea swayed amidst the outsized waves.<br /> <br /> Wahine was the only one who remained conscious long enough to see the sky go dark as the moon rose to blot out the sun.<br /> <br /> <b>The Forest Near the Tomb of the Stone Maw, RY 767, 23rd of Ascending Fire, Half an Hour After Sunrise:</b><br /> <br /> Pakari had plenty of warning. As he ran, searching for the Bearer of Bones, he heard the raucous forest once again grow quiet, and he watched as the little spirits fled through the treetops...again, away from the tomb he was running towards. He had already endured the shaking of the earth this morning.<br /> <br /> ...he was still unprepared for the intensity of it when it hit. The sound of tree trunks splintering and shattering as they twisted under the buckling earth filled his ears with ringing as he stumbled and tried to catch himself. Great cracks appeared in the soil, and strangely colored smoke rose from under the earth and assaulted his senses with wavering vision and stinging skin and the smell of bad eggs and burning. There was a brief moment of stillness as the earth paused in its shuddering...and then a hot wind picked Pakari and the trees near him up like dolls and tossed him into some more trees, and everything was pain, and bright light, and the smell of honey...<br /> <br /> <b>???????</b><br /> <br /> The Maiden was asking the locals permission for her friends from Captain Phi Ho's ship to dock and rest in their village, and as she spoke she felt the hot sand burning through her footwear and up onto the soles of her feet...it was getting more and more uncomfortable...and suddenly the heat roared up her legs to surround her whole body, and she felt herself surrounded by flames, and the sky turned dark, and the only sounds were the crackling of flames and the clanking of the chains glowing orange on her ankles and wrists as she thrashed, and a deep, rumbling voice which whispered in her ear.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000080\">OaThbrEAker!</span> </i>The voice whispered, and something huge and dark moved beyond the flames. <span style=\"color:#000080\"><i>OuR belOved <span style=\"font-size:9px\">oh so bEloved</span> dauGH! ..ter has <u><span style=\"font-size:14px\">returned </span></u>arrived <span style=\"font-size:8px\">faLlen </span>come <u>back </u>to us aaAAAH! ...nd after <b>WE </b>had alMOst given up<span style=\"font-size:9px\"> <u>gone </u>to sleEp</span> abandoned <span style=\"font-size:14px\">hope</span>!</i></span> <span style=\"color:#000080\"><i>oAThBreaKer! Oathbreaker!</i></span><br /> <br /> The shape in the darkness rose, and rose, and somewhere beyond the roaring of the flames and the searing of her skin she could see apair of <i>eyes, </i>eyes blazing in red and orange and wavering shapes like twin suns, and they were <i>looking at her</i>, they could <i>see</i> her, and a black claw the size of the world reached out to her, and-<br /> <br /> <b>Somewhere With Soft Green Light and The Smell of Flowers, ???, ???</b><br /> <br /> Pakari was abruptly awoken by the sound of a woman he did not know screaming in absolute terror. It was the sort of sound that rouses most people, no matter how much they and their aching bodies would like to keep sleeping. It roused Seskan too (who almost fell off of a couch he had been laid upon), and woke Wahine with a sudden start that had her immediately wincing at the pain in her broken ribs.<br /> <br /> The hand that had been reaching for the Maiden to wipe he brow pulled back in distress, and a gentle voice spoke. &quot;It's alright, child. It's alright. It was a dream, and your dreams are not the ones that hold power here.&quot;<br /> <br /> Scattered moans and groans drew attention to the other wounded who had been gathered in this...where was this? It appeared to be a stone grotto, or a cave with a roof open to the sky. Flowering vines hung down into the cave, and the color of the sky meant the sun was either rising or setting...they were surrounded by men and women who were wearing bandages or splints. Pakari recognized a bundle with a child's mummified hand sticking out of it propped in a corner: the bones were here, but he did not see their Bearer. Seskan, sitting up, found that he was wearing a splint on his leg and it hurt to put any weight on it. The Maiden, coming slowly out of her nightmare, recognized Wahine on a wood-and-rushes cot. Her adorable rabbit-eared companion was nowhere to be found.<br /> <br /> Several warriors with intricate geometric tattoos in white, black, and red stood silently around the periphery of the chamber, their eyes darting from person to person. A tall, graceful man with skin the color of gold and hair the pink and purple of a glorious sunset had a bowl of cool water and a compress, and had been attempting to bring down the Maiden's fever.<br /> <br /> &quot;I am glad you woke up,&quot; he smiled, and his smiling was like the sun coming out after a bad storm (even if his teeth and his ears were just a little too pointed). &quot;You were really burning up there. That fever had me worried.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Aaaand now you're all together, after an indefinite period of unconsciousness. Wahine, take 3 Bashing. Seskan, take 1L. Pakari, take 2 Bashing. Maiden's miraculously uninjured...physically, anyway. Time for plots to thicken.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 02-27-2015, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T11:15:41-08:00","id":421972,"title":"","content":"Pakari tried to sit up, grunted, laid back down, and then attempted to rise again, slowly. He was more successful this time, despite the fact that it felt like every part of him hurt. It was the second time in as many years that he had been tossed around by the elements and knocked unconscious, and he started to wonder if this would become a regular occurrence.<br /> <br /> Parki closed his eyes, trying to focus. He had been running for the Tomb... he had paused because he thought he saw the bearer of the bones... then the earth split, and the wind picked him up and threw him, and after that he had no idea what happened. Part of him was desperately worried for Master Hasya, and wondered what was happening to the island, but it was difficult to concentrate on anything except the immediate present. He shook his head, futilely trying to clear it, and looked around. He did not recognize this place or any of the people here. The warriors were probably Whispering Valley tribe, if the tattoos were anything to go by... but he could not be in the Whispering Valley, could he? He had been clear on the other side of the island! Pakari's mind reeled from confusion and headache.<br /> <br /> Soon enough, it came to him that there was a simple way to learn what was going on. Pakari turned to face the golden-skinned man* and tried to speak. At first he just croaked - his mouth was so dry... how long had he been asleep? - but after swallowing a few times, he managed to get out the words &quot;Where are we? Who are you?&quot; in a passibly intelligible manner.<br /> <br /> *<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Was it a man? Pakari had never seen a man with gold skin before. Maybe it was a spirit. He seemed solid enough. Perhaps one of the gods' children or grandchildren? The hair reminded Pakari of something, but at the moment his thoughts were not clear enough to guide him...</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T22:47:21-08:00","id":422629,"title":"","content":"&quot;You are safe,&quot; the golden-skinned man said, and his voice was the smell of honey. Pakari found it deeply familiar, he had been smelling it in his sleep. &quot;At least for now. We are in a hidden grotto in the mountains west of the Temple of Eyes, and the warriors of the Whispering Valley assure me that the wards here should hold even after nightfall...and I have the honor to be Endlessly Yearning Horizon, a humble poet in the service of The Gleaming Prince. You hit your head, so please don't try to stand just yet...how many fingers am I holding up?&quot;<br /> <br /> The golden-skinned man put down the cold compress in a bowl next to the Maiden, and held his hands up for Pakari. He was holding up six fingers on his right hand and two fingers on his left hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T06:41:51-08:00","id":422863,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/vqybsjj.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <br /> Her head hurt and it seem like there is thousand of cicadas singing in it without any kind of rhythm or reason, her body felt sore, she didn't remember having a any kind of flu this morning, isn't she ?<br /> <br /> Everything is so chaotic right now, one moment she was with her master and now she is lying in what she think is a cave, the rocky ground is cold to the touch, she can see creeping vines hang from the cave's walls like inanimate snakes. The Maiden saw the islander from the beach also lied not too far from her, and she can see above both of them is a hole on the cave's ceiling which revealed the sky, though she is not sure whether it's dawn or dusk right now.<br /> <br /> Now that she think about it, the islanders were lying in some kind of wooden bed which look so uncomfortable, but her is so soft and warm, and then a voice like that of honey spoke to her, and that is when the Maiden realized that she is resting her head in a man lap, a golden skin and sunset colored hair man to be exact, before she could respond by screaming and roiling around the stone floor the man turned his attention to something else. It looked like one of the islander is questioning the golden man.<br /> <br /> Strange, since the Maiden didn't remembered seeing him on the beach at all. And then he asked the islander how many fingers is he seeing, it's one of those test to see whether an individual has regained their sense if she remembered correctly. It would be impolite to answer for the burly islander so the Maiden decided to just sit patiently on that wonderful and warm lap for the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T12:50:25-08:00","id":423331,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">At first, there was just a dull ache as consciousness floated at the edge of wakefulness. Then, as a blood curdling sound of terror jolted her upright, there was only excruciating pain. She yelped silently, hand going to her side reflexively, breathing sharp and shallow through tightly clenched teeth, eyes tearing as the sensation passed . There was no mistaking the pain in her side for anything other than broken ribs. How many she was not sure. She'd always heard breaking a rib was one of the most painful experiences a person could endure, mostly because there wasn't a damn thing anyone could do about it and every jostle, every breath was a painful reminder of injury. She was having a hard time disagreeing. Painful, yes, life threatening... doubtful, as long as she took it easy and didn't get bumped around too much as her bones began stitching themselves back together. She wasn't a doctor but she assumed if she could still breath normally, albeit not without some pain if she inhaled too deeply, then it must have been a clean break. She pawed clumsily for her staff to lean on. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Settled upright, the pain receded to a tolerable ache. She looked around, utterly bewildered. She recognized some of the others but the strange tattooed individuals where a complete mystery. She'd heard of tattooed warriors that lived on the far side but why would they be here? Her gaze was suddenly drawn to the unusual man in the room, eyes becoming fixated on the golden stranger whose pleasant honeyed words filled her head with the scent of delightful sweetness. For a fleeting second, she felt soothed by his presence, that she could loose herself in the gentle warmth of that honey scented sound. But something deep in the back of her mind, some part of her momentarily forgotten, was deeply unsettled. When he flashed his fingers at a nearby man she'd never seen, she jumped painfully to her to her feet. Wincing through gritted teeth as she leaned on her staff there was a flicker of fear in her eyes as she glared distrustfully. Her hand clutched the iron pendent in her necklace as she breathed in shallow breaths and waited for the pain of another sudden jostle to pass.<br /> <br /> <i>What are you?</i> She mouthed silently through narrowed, apprehensive eyes. She hoped he was a god or spirit that meant no harm but she would not let her guard down on a hope. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","user":"Foxsimile","date":". 02-28-2015, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T09:08:02-08:00","id":424202,"title":"","content":"The gold-skinned man, still holding his generously fingered hands up for Pakari, turned and gave Wahine a sharp-toothed smile.<br /> <br /> &quot;Winking Balor, but that's some delicious fear! Other than our feverish guest here, the room was a bit bland, so you have my thanks...but I assure you it's not necessary. You're perfectly safe...hm. None of your injuries were to your throat or larynx. I didn't think your ribs were bad enough to impede your breathing...and, while I assure you I mean absolutely no offense,&quot; his gorgeous face turned slightly sheepish as his voice grew thoughtful, &quot;You taste a bit funny. Your fear has sort of a salty flavor, like you used to be...even braver...and a mute...are you one of Tarana's pets, by chance? I'm surprised, she doesn't usually let you lot leave the Court of Dying Winds.&quot;<br /> <br /> The tattooed warrior nearest to Endlessly Yearning Horizon, as he called himself, placed his hand on the hilt of an obsidian sword and scowled at the strange healer, who for his part gave the warrior a wink and a shrug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 03-01-2015, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:16:05-08:00","id":425534,"title":"","content":"Pakari blinked and spoke his first impression: &quot;You have six fingers on your right hand.&quot; Then was a brief pause while Pakari reorganized his thoughts and answered &quot;I mean, eight. Eight in all.&quot;<br /> <br /> Things were beginning to become clearer - Endlessly Yearning Horizon was probably one of the strange folk from the Empty Sail or Honey Islands, which would explain both his odd appearance and behavior handily. How he came to be here, doing healing work for the Whispering Valley tribe, would probably make for a good story by itself, but right now that was not what Pakari wanted to know about. He wanted to know why he was in this cave, what happened to Hasya, and what was happening to Whitestone Island in that order.<br /> <br /> &quot;How did I get here? I was over in the jungle by Windrest... Did the wind carry me all the way here?&quot;<br /> <br /> It was a stupid question, and Pakari realized it shortly after the words left his mouth. He felt he knew a little about flying and falling, and was pretty confident that if he had really been thrown by the wind for dozens of miles, he should be dead. The alternative was that he had landed somewhere else and then been carried here while he was knocked out, but that just raised more questions...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T02:37:03-08:00","id":426342,"title":"","content":"&quot;No, he did.&quot; Endlessly Yearning Horizon nodded in the direction of one of the tattooed warriors, who was <i>almost</i> as large as Pakari himself. &quot;He and his men were sent to investigate a tomb out in the jungle once the earthquakes started, the Whispering Valley Tribe's Temple Guardians thought they might be connected somehow. They found you in the area and brought you back for questioning. Speaking of which...you didn't by any chance free the ancient man-eating demon that guards that tomb, did you? We've got wards up against the dead, but I'm not sure about demons.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T06:23:27-08:00","id":426502,"title":"","content":"Pakari closed his eyes and started rubbing his forehead. His first instinct was to blurt out questions he could guess the answers to, but that would not help him now. He took a breath, and concentrated on speaking deliberately when he answered Horizon next. &quot;Master Hasya was at the Tomb of the Stone Maw to check the wards, make sure the demon was still trapped inside. I am his apprentice. He sent me to get some supplies because the wards were looking worn after the storm. When the earth started shaking, I doubled back to make sure he was alright.... I hadn't reached the tomb before... something happened. It felt like the entire island was coming apart, and I was knocked out.&quot;<br /> <br /> Pakari opened his eyes and started scanning the warriors around the room, especially the large one, to see if they had any reaction. &quot;Did anyone go to the tomb?&quot; he asked of no one in particular. &quot;What happened there?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 03-03-2015, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T20:17:50-08:00","id":427286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/239065-ic-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign?p=424202#post424202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">&quot;Winking Balor, but that's some delicious fear! Other than our feverish guest here, the room was a bit bland, so you have my thanks...but I assure you it's not necessary. You're perfectly safe...hm. None of your injuries were to your throat or larynx. I didn't think your ribs were bad enough to impede your breathing...and, while I assure you I mean absolutely no offense,&quot; his gorgeous face turned slightly sheepish as his voice grew thoughtful, &quot;You taste a bit funny. Your fear has sort of a salty flavor, like you used to be...even braver...and a mute...are you one of Tarana's pets, by chance? I'm surprised, she doesn't usually let you lot leave the Court of Dying Winds.&quot;</span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Wahine bristled visibly with a sudden, complex flurry of emotion. At first, utter revulsion that he could taste some part of her essence, then revulsion gave way to an anger that overpowered that quick jolt of fear that had spurred her to her feet. How dare he taste her much less talk about it aloud in such a flippant manner! The sudden change in his beautiful features, that shift to something softer with a hint of coyness, that soothing sweet voice melting into something gentler and thoughtful... it made her chest flutter until the content of his words struck her like a bolt of lightening. First, it was a shock to hear him speak so casually about something that had never been spoken aloud and had never been shared in great detail. Second, to hear that the monster from her past had a name and had left a taste on her soul... she felt as if she'd been thrown into an icy sea. Then a flash of anger at being called a pet and the insinuation that her escape was nothing more than the whim of a fairfolk who'd grown bored with her new toy. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Though the fateful night itself was a blur from glamour and the passage of time, she remembered vividly the fevered nights where strange siren songs called to her in a voice she knew was once hers. Over time, those strange fits, fevers, and symptoms of invisible wounds faded. But half a lifetime forced to communicate through vivid expression and bold body language left unfiltered emotions boiling much closer to the surface than if she had layers of communication to obfuscate her deeper feelings. She wondered sometimes if that </span></span><i>monster,</i><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Tarana he'd called her... maybe she had pulled some part of her closer to the surface when she'd pulled at her soul and ripped her voice from her lips. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Again his honeyed words filled her head as he turned to speak to a man she couldn't recall ever seeing before. She shook the distraction from her mind, scowling at the fairfolk once more from her defensive stance. </span></span><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Why are we </i><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>here?&quot; S</i>he barked silently, glaring daggers. &quot;<i>What do you want with us?&quot; </i>She pointed her staff at the fairfolk, emboldened by the iron pendent against her skin. It seemed he could understand her and from the stories she'd heard of the silent tribe, perhaps they too where skilled at reading the words on her lips. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","user":"Foxsimile","date":". 03-03-2015, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T05:49:52-08:00","id":427641,"title":"","content":"The golden man smiled at Wahine. &quot;I'm here to treat the wounded. You're here because you were wounded. The Whispering Valley tribe is trying to figure out what set off the earthquakes today. You were with the group that was on the beach when the easterners showed up on their ship. They think the easterners might be responsible, so they gathered up your group. He's here,&quot; and here the golden man nodded at Pakari, &quot; because he was found near an ancient tomb they think is linked with the earthquakes, I don't know all the details.&quot;<br /> <br /> He shrugged again, and his sunset-colored hair bounced perfectly without losing its tousled and graceful shape.<br /> <br /> &quot;If you're asking why the Whispering Valley Tribe hasn't just murdered me with iron and white stone...a cynic would say they don't wish to give my Lord an excuse to come out of retirement to avenge me. Perhaps I'm being vain, but I prefer to think we've developed some actual bonds of friendship during my exile to your island...as for what I want with you, I'd be grateful if you could be maybe a little less angry? It's like being force-fed bitter roots.&quot;<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, one of the large tattooed warriors approached in response to Pakari's questions. His voice was quiet and deep and a little raspy.<br /> <br /> &quot;You are Pakari, correct? We found your master's possessions near the Tomb of the Stone Maw, but he was nowhere to be found. The Maw was split open by the earthquake. Our Temple Guardian wouldn't let us anyone venture inside to see if the guardian monster was still inside, since that was what freed it last time. He spent a few hours there looking and just returned some time ago. He suspects the wards may have been broken, but his studies focus on the dead. We're assuming the demon got free, though. Most of our people are going into hiding behind stone walls. If it's really free, we'll find out tonight. The stories say last time it was released it summoned storms to blot out the heavens.&quot;<br /> <br /> Endlessly Yearning Horizon frowned at that. It was <i>adorable</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;I wish you'd told me that. I plan on living a few more millennia, and hungry demons are exactly the sort of thing that can interfere with those sorts of plans.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You told me just this morning that you love surprises, Fair One.&quot; The tattooed warrior grinned darkly and chuckled. &quot;It would have been <i>rude</i> of me to ruin this one for you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Endlessly Yearning Horizon glared at him furiously. This, too, was adorable.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T13:03:31-08:00","id":428024,"title":"","content":"Pakari stood up so he could look the warrior in the eye, and grimaced. He tried to ignore the pain, reminding himself that it was only bruising. &quot;Have there been any more earthquakes since...&quot; Pakari paused as he tried to consider the time. It was easily two or three days walking from Windrest to Whispering Valley, and it had been early in the morning when the first quake struck. Now it was twilight again... Pakari couldn't guess whether the sun was East or West from this vantage point. If the warriors had run day and night, they might have covered the distance more quickly, which would mean at least one day had passed. But would they wouldn't move so hastily if they were moving injured people, would they?<br /> <br /> &quot;...the first one? How long was I asleep?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 03-04-2015, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T09:03:37-08:00","id":430359,"title":"","content":"Her social sense is tingling, such tenseness hanging in the air after the man spoke about something that concern the mute woman, the way he talks with such a nonchalantly tone make it seem as if he's delighted in getting a reaction out of people.<br /> <br /> Now that she thought about it, who exactly is the &quot;<span style=\"color:#800080\">oathbreaker</span>&quot; that the voice refer to back then ? Perhaps she has betrayed someone in her past life and now their ghost is now seeking revenge upon her ? That seem.......too much like fiction, it's true that real life is often stranger than you think, but she wouldn't be that unlucky to be the main character in some kind of ghost horror novel, would she ? But the voice also mention &quot;<span style=\"color:#800080\">daughter</span>&quot;, and the Maiden remembered that the voice said &quot;<span style=\"color:#800080\">returns</span>&quot; in its rambling as well, the Maiden always thought that she is just a random normal girl with amnesia whose parent are so clumsy that they forget they left their daughter on a slaver's ship, but being a daughter of some<i>thing</i> on this island, that is just a little too much for what she expect.<br /> <br /> But the catastrophe happened right after she set foot on the island so.......wait, did somebody just said that the islander was blaming her master and the Captain's crews for the earthquake.......<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;Whaaaaaaaaaaat !&quot;</span>, neither her master nor the crew know the islander's language, they don't know the islander's custom either, this is a recipe for disaster ! If either sides initiates hostility then it can only end in bloodbath.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#800080\">Mister. I n</span>.....I...I mean, everyone, please kindly let me get back to the beach, none of companions knows the island's language, and the people will certainly be angry at my friends who will get blamed for the catastrophe just now.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T06:25:30-07:00","id":432573,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#4B0082\">&quot;Oh, she speaks Old Realm!&quot;</span> Endlessly Yearning Horizon once more turned to the Maiden. <span style=\"color:#4B0082\">&quot;And with only a hint of a provincial accent. It feels so good to speak with someone cultured after all this time babbling in the inbred bastardization of ancient Seatongue that passes for 'language' on this misbegotten island! Please, lady, calm yourself. It pains me to see such a beautiful face distorted by worry. Your friends are safe. The wyld-twisted one with the amusing ears sprained his ankle and lost his hat in the earthquake, but the others are fine. They are currently being held captive by the Whispering Valley tribe's warriors. I've served twice as a translator for them. They are in good health, are being fed and treated well, and obviously know nothing of the earthquake. Your cat-faced captain is threatening to shell the island with cannon if we don't hand the lot of you over to him by sunrise, but I think he's bluffing. His fur stood up straight as soon as he saw me. Poor man must have been treated poorly in the past by my kindred. He doesn't know how many of the Raksha are on the island, and I think he's afraid to attack without more information. Cold iron can only do so much good, you know...&quot;</span><br /> <br /> &quot;There have been several small quakes. The first one was this morning. Our...guest...here,&quot; the tattooed warrior nodded to the golden man who was delightedly chattering at the Maiden, &quot;loaned us his pet monster...he calls it his <i>steed...</i>to survey the island more quickly. It can fly faster than our gliders, and carry a dozen men. It's out now with some of our better spotters searching for your Master, or for any any others injured by the quake. It was mostly centered in the jungle. Lots of fallen trees, and some houses were damaged, but not too many people were hurt, or they were hurt near to their own families and their own healers.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T01:40:19-07:00","id":442330,"title":"","content":"Wahine relaxed gradually as the others talked. Her posture no longer bristled visibly and her expressions became more controlled. She regarded the fair folk with mild caution, the way a creature might cautiously regard a predator that, for the moment at least, didn't seem particularly hungry or interested in giving chase. The fair folk did seem to have some sort of rapport with the tribesmen which eased her mind slightly. Truth be told, in the deepest darkest parts of her mind beneath the memory of mortal terror, she did find something magnetic about the fair folk and their strange magics. Glimpses of gossamer spun treasures beyond anything she might replicate within a lifetime of mortal toil was both a source of inspiration and deepest artistic frustration. She'd never actually <i>been</i> in the presence of a fair folk with her wits intact; never had the opportunity to really interact with one on if not exactly peaceful terms then at least neutral terms. Assuaged of her initial fear, she was actually kind of... fascinated, though she tried to keep it to herself as best as she could. There where more important matters she could focus on to keep from being drawn in by the creature's magnetic pull. She focused her attention on the tribesmen to distract her.<br /> <br /> <i>'<b>If a demon has been freed and the earthquake was an omen of things to come, then we should take whatever action we can.' </b></i> Wahine signed quickly as she mouthed the words at a normal speaking speed. It seemed she was amongst company that could understand her far more clearly then the average person of the villages she frequented. How long had it been since she could 'speak' at a normal pace in a minimally restricted manner? No pantomiming, no need to constrain herself to simple sentences and key words spoken painfully slow. The thought of it excited her. She tried not to let her excitement show too much. <b>'</b><i><b>\u200bYou seem to know a lot about this demon creature and what it's capable of. I will follow your lead.&quot;</b></i><br /> <br /> She paused, thinking of the others. '<b><i>perhaps the Easterners have useful tools. A large ship probably has at least some useful goods for trading. Maybe those goods would be useful for our purposes'</i></b><br /> <br /> Secretly she also just wanted an excuse to board that beautiful vessel. Preferably with the captain's consent which reminded her... &quot;<b><i>I'd like to meet this captain if there's time. His consent may be useful. Hardened seamen are useful in a fight as well. I... understand </i></b><b><i>sea tongue if that's helpful.&quot;</i> </b>There was no use in hiding it. Fighting a demon came far before being able to eavesdrop on the new arrivals to get the upper hand on a trade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T07:54:07-07:00","id":442520,"title":"","content":"<b><i>'I like that plan.'</i> </b>The tattooed warrior who had been speaking to Pakari signed back to Wahine. <i><b>'We can always use more warriors, and I'd rather send strangers to fight the demon than risk my own men. We will have you and the strange woman who came with them negotiate with them for us after sunrise. It is too late to do it now, and it is not safe to be out tonight. The earthquakes broke more wards than those on the demon, and our priests are expecting the hungry dead will be out in force tonight, even if the demon does not show up.'</b></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T12:07:17-07:00","id":442918,"title":"","content":"Wahine's face lit up when the warriors responded promptly without a single question of clarification or a single puzzled look. And in sign no less! How sweet and how rare to speak clearly and naturally! It was no different then the sweet relief of seeing other people after long periods in uninhabited lands. She cast her glance aside as she centered her thoughts once more, thinking deeply about the matter at hand.<br /> <br /> '<i><b>Well I suppose we are stuck here for the night at least'</b></i> she sighed, her side aching dully. Her body was already instinctively adjusting to her injury; distributing weight away from pressuring her wound, avoiding unnecessary motion of her upper body, other muscles compensating for her chest and torso to minimize the push and pull against her unset bones.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i><b>Maiden,&quot; </b></i> she said with a kindly smile, kneeling carefully so the she could look the girl in the eye and slowly mouth every word. She signed too, so that the tribesmen could see what she was saying and perhaps fill in communication gaps. &quot;<i><b>Tell me of your </b></i><b><i>captain. I want to know him better so I can more easily calm his worries. Stories would pass the time until morning.&quot; </i></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","user":"Foxsimile","date":". 03-15-2015, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T22:55:00-07:00","id":445399,"title":"","content":"She turned to look at young man she was sure she'd never met before. <i><b>'Pakari is it? Would you or your master know of a Master Susilo in Green River?&quot;</b></i><br /> <br /> It wasn't unusual for people to visit Susilo's workshop looking for raw materials of utilitarian, artistic, or spiritual purposes. At least locally it was well known that Susilo was the first person to go to if you needed something. Wahine had a knack for procuring valuable materials that kept Susilo's storeroom well stocked. Perhaps they had visited Master Susilo at some point in the past for goods and supplies.<br /> <br /> <i><b>'I'm not sure what is needed to repair the wards or bind a demon but he might have something useful for spiritual rituals.'</b></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T05:13:19-07:00","id":447582,"title":"","content":"It's good that the men are being treated well the the local, but her Master getting lost in the earthquake is worrisome to the Maiden, she can only pray from the bottom of her heart for the moon and the star to guide her Master to somewhere safe and not into a rabbit stew.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hmmm, the captain ?&quot;, one of the tattoo warrior lightly tapped the Maiden on her shoulder to translate Wahine's question toward the girl. With her finger put on her chin, the Maiden made a puzzled look, now that she thought about it, who exactly is Captain Phi Ho anyway ? All she knew was that the Captain has been her Master friend ever since they found her on that abandoned ship, she never really spoke to the man until recently when she boarded his ship to sailed to this island.<br /> <br /> Aye, isn't it just embarrassing when a stranger ask who your companion is and all you know is their name. &quot;Well, the captain is.......&quot;, the girl took a stick and draw some sort of doodle that look like a tiger face on a patch of dirt near Wahine, &quot;...a giant tigerman, so you should recognized him the moment you meet all the crew.&quot;, resting her slightly titled head on her knee the Maiden continued, &quot;He's your typical man of the sea. Boisterous, rowdy, always refer to his ship as if it is a lover, fatherly loving his crew, stuff like that.&quot;. The raven-haired girl smiled awkwardly at Wahine, &quot;Sorry, that's all I know, I have only spoken to him a few week ago.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hmmm, Wahine seem friendly enough, and there's only a few people here. The Maiden wonder whether she should speak to Wahine about the vision and that the earthquake early may have some connection to her arrival to the island.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T08:59:38-07:00","id":447749,"title":"","content":"Pakari turned away from the warrior, rubbing his eyes and trying to think. He was, to be frank, completely at a loss about what to do next. This situation was seemingly completely out of his control, and Hasya wasn't around to give him instructions. The obvious next step was to go look for him, but the search was out of his hands.<br /> <br /> He turned out the conversation between Horizon and the young girl - later, he would realize that they had been speaking the language of the gods (which Hasya had not yet taught him), and wonder how they both knew it. For now, he stewed in his own thoughts, trying and failing to come up with any plan that didn't involve waiting.<br /> '<br /> Eventually, he became aware that the other woman, the one with exaggerated body language, was standing in front of him and trying to 'speak.' Pakari blinked at her, confused. He did not understand hand signs, and it took a few seconds to realize she was mouthing words. &quot;Uhh... Su... si... lo? Susilo the shipwright? Yes, I know him. I visit him, sometimes.&quot;In fact, Pakari used to earn extra bread for his aunt and himself by doing odd jobs for the old carpenter, and had learned a little about his craft. Nowadays, they rarely saw each other if Pakari wasn't shopping on Hasya's behalf.<br /> <br /> &quot;I was going to get some rope and other things from him earlier today, but it's probably pointless now. To bind a demon, we'd need talismans...&quot; he paused, trying to remember his lessons. &quot;...the best thing for talismans is engraved whitestone, but that's expensive and takes time to prepare. Carved bone works well, or even inked wood in the short term. Depending on what you're binding or warding, you may also need incense, salt, or iron.&quot; Pakari's eyes involuntarily flicked towards Endlessly Yearning Horizon. &quot;Susilo probably has some of those things, and I can get the rest from Hohepa... I'm sorry, but I'm having trouble understanding you. Can you read and write?&quot;<br /> <br /> That the woman apparently could not speak was odd, but it wasn't the strangest thing Pakari had seen today by far. For now, it was just another obstacle he'd have to find a way around in order to accomplish anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T23:05:34-07:00","id":448878,"title":"","content":"Wahine nodded when Pakari read the name on her lips. When he asked if she could read or write, she wrote 'yes' on the ground. Unfortunately she didn't have any parchment on her. Or a writing utensil. She would just have to etch simple words in the dust and dirt with her bare fingers. She carefully traced her name onto the ground and gestured to herself, hoping he could read her writing clearly. <br /> <br /> <b>W-A-H-I-N-E </b><br /> <br /> The same as Susilo's quiet, aloof assistant who never seemed to speak to anyone and only rarely looked up from her work. <br /> <br /> She smiled as she watched the Maiden scratch drawings in the sand. A tiger man eh? She filed that in her memory. That could potentially be very useful. Had he always been a tiger man? Was it something imposed on him later in life through the whims of a fair folk like her own affliction? Her mind began to mull over several scenarios. There wasn't much more that could be done that evening. In the morning, if there was time, she would grab some of her finest crafts from her workshop at Susilo's. She'd seen the sorts of things that seafaring traders salivated over. A promise of reward was no match for a visual example of the sorts of riches she could trade for their willing assistance. Until the morning at least, they could all stand some rest. The ache in her side begged for stillness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T18:26:20-07:00","id":452200,"title":"","content":"As our injured heroes got to know one another, and slowly and groaningly figured out how to move and converse around their wounds both physical and supernatural, Endlessly Yearning Horizon tended to the other wounded from the earthquake, several of whom similarly woke up and began chattering with one another (and several of whom were also terrified of the golden-skinned extra-fingered emotion-tasting healer, and needed to be gently talked down).<br /> <br /> The sun slowly set, and the sky overhead turned purple before fading to a deep dark blue studded with several gleaming stars. The flowers on the vines that grew on the walls of the grotto slowly closed, and the constant background noise of distant birds quieted, and the tattooed guards lit a couple of torches in sconces on the grotto walls. The atmosphere in the grotto was tense, for everyone in the little grotto got the news that a demon was loose and the earthquake had injured people and broken ancient wards guarding the island from the dead and evil spirits, but they took to Wahine's suggestion and passed the time with stories.<br /> <br /> A young woman named Tulani told a story about her grandmother meeting Oihana of the Silent Wood when she was lost in the jungles of the north as a girl, and how her ancestor had persuaded the god to show her the way home in exchange for the answer to a riddle. A young warrior with red and black and white tattoos who introduced himself as Kune asked Pakari for news of the Bearer of Bones, who had not been found in the shattered jungle, though the bones she bore had been recovered. He thanked Pakari for what news he could give, and he took the small corpse out of the grotto and away into one of the caves, his eyes wet in the torchlight. Endlessly Yearning Horizon, as the hour grew late, finished with most of his medical ministrations, told a tale of a mighty warrior-princess who fought a thousand battles and won a thousand victories, until one day she stood across the field from the queen of an enemy kingdom and fell in love with her foe. The princess lost her first battle, for the queen she faced was a brilliant strategist and a peerless swordswoman, and thereafter the princess became cruel and vicious, mounting assault after assault in the hopes of facing again the only enemy who had ever brought her low. The story ended with the queen's sword in the princess's heart and a smile on the princess' face, and it should have been a tragedy (especially with the subplot Horizon worked in about how the warrior-queen was married to an old bitter tyrant of a husband), but the way the golden-skinned man told it everyone was smiling at the end, for the princess had found the ending she desired.<br /> <br /> The Maiden took a turn at the telling of tales then, for nobody else seemed confident enough to follow the burning words of the gold-skinned healer, but the Maiden was a professional storyteller and she got up and did the voices and acted out the parts and if Menreiki-San would have rolled his eyes and told her she just couldn't go deep enough to get the villain's voice right and her timing in the third act was terrible, it didn't matter, for she was telling stories of strange distant lands none of these islanders had ever heard of, and stories unlike any they knew. Several times she had to stop and explain things like taxes and towers and ice and silk in the middle of her narrative, and as she spoke her listeners' eyes grew wide with wonder as their imagination brought them to places they had never known existed. Endlessly Yearning Horizon smiled and Wahine noticed him licking his lips as the Maiden spoke and her audience listened in wonder, and occasionally making happy little humming noises like a child sucking on candy.<br /> <br /> At one point, somebody brought out a flute, and there was music, and while he was a little bit clumsy at first, after the first time Pakari lifted someone up and twirled them around over his head he was suddenly the most popular dance partner in the tiny little cave. Grown men and women waited their turn to be spun about as they had not been since they were children, until finally Pakari's head spun and Horizon politely asked him to sit down before he fell over and got<i> another</i> concussion, and took his place among the dancers.<br /> <br /> Eventually, after many tales had been told and the torches were guttering low, and the night had grown cool, everyone finally decided to rest. With grunts and moans of pain forgotten during the telling of tails, they grabbed the bedrolls provided by the Whispering Valley Tribe and found their cots and joined their companions who had already fallen to slumber. Endlessly Yearning Horizon stalked quietly from cot to cot like a concerned hen, occasionally touching two fingers to a sleeping man's neck to check his pulse if his breathing was slow, or pausing as still as a golden statue to listen to breathing or a heartbeat before moving on. As the others drifted into their dreams, Wahine clutched her pittance of iron close, and remembered a cold night under strange stars and the lapping of waves and unearthly music... and could not make herself sleep, try as she might. She pretended to sleep, and listened to Horizon's quiet pacing, and listened to the guards.<br /> <br /> There were two passages out of the grotto, both winding away out of sight into the rough black stone of the mountain. Several times tattooed warriors came in or out and signed to each other. Wahine gathered from glimpses at their hands moving in the dying torchlight that this location seemed secure, but that the dead were out in much greater numbers than usual in the Whispering Valley. Most of the Whispering Valley Tribe had safely been evacuated from the villages during daylight, and now they were safely ensconced behind the heavily warded walls of the Temple of Eyes or the Hall of Singing Stones. A fierce battle was apparently raging at the Village of Stairs, as the permanent wards etched into the stone walls there had cracked during the earthquake. Periodic reports on the fighting came in as the night wore on. Several hours before morning, a report came in that gliders had succeeded in scattering enough salt bombs to disperse and drive off the dead, buying the Village of Stairs enough time to repair the damaged wards.<br /> <br /> Endlessly Yearning Horizon finally approached Wahine and told her in a gentle whisper that Pakari (asleep and snoring gently on a nearby cot) was dreaming frankly <i>delicious</i> dreams about flying and wrestling giant eels and making his aunt an eelskin purse as a present, far tastier than anything Wahine's battered little husk of a soul could manage even if she wasn't all terrified and bitter-tasting, and that he swore on his very Heart he wasn't going to come over and eat any of her soul in her sleep. He asked one of the tattooed warriors to stand on guard next her cot, and wake her if the golden skinned healer so much as approached them. After Horizon left, the guard (a young woman who introduced herself as Kiri) smiled at her and showed her a white jade dagger carved in the shape of a shark, and told her it was carved by an ancestor who named it Dreamslayer because he used it to slay a faerie raider. The dagger had been passed down in her family for six generations, and each successive bearer of the blade had slain one more Raksha than the previous bearer. Kiri grinned cruelly and nodded at Endlessly Yearning Horizon on the other side of the room, and told Wahine she had a legacy to live up to, and she sorta <i>hoped</i> the healer tried to steal her soul in her sleep. It would give her an <i>excuse.</i><br /> <br /> After that, she slept soundly until sunrise.<br /> <br /> <b>Green Moon Grotto, RY 767, 24th of Ascending Fire, Sunrise</b><br /> <br /> Morning came with the sound of quiet talking. As the Maiden awoke and sat up, rubbing away sleep, she got smiles and friendly nods from friends she had made the night before.<br /> <br /> &quot;Would you mind waking Wahine?&quot; Endlessly Yearning Horizon asked her, handing her a hot clay bowl full of stewed yams and sweet fruit. &quot;Our, um, prisoners have woken up, and apparently it's time to take you all back to your cat-faced captain. I'd wake her myself, but there's a legend there I'd rather not become a part of.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Pakari?&quot; Kune, the tattooed warrior who had taken away the Bearer's bones the night before, spoke to Pakari as he ate his breakfast, feeling much better than he had the previous day. &quot;We're riding out soon on Endlessly Yearning Horizon's flying beast. After we talk to the Maiden's strange friends from her distant land, the plan is to fly north to search the Tomb of the Stone Maw for your master or the Bearer of Bones, and maybe see if we can find the demons' tracks. If the stories are true, it sleeps by day, so we're hoping we can trap it or poison it before it awakes again at sunset. We'd be happy to have you along.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>OOC:<br /> You have had a good night's rest, tended to by an attentive healer. Pakari, you are fully healed and in good shape again. Wahine, you've had time to heal 2B, but your rib (which is mending really fast and well due to Horizon's expert care) is still sore, especially if you breathe hard or twist or touch it-you've still got 1B on you. Seskan, if you're still with us, your 1L has fully healed and you are feeling much better this morning.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 03-22-2015, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T08:01:20-07:00","id":452691,"title":"","content":"Ah, the Maiden felt bad for having such a joyous night yesterday while her Master is still missing, if they all get back to the mainland alive then she will definitely use all the money that she kept to treat him with a big banquet. The Maiden slowly crawled toward Wahine, it's seem that she and Horizon don't get along very well, why anyone would hate such a charming man like Horizon is a mystery to the Maiden.<br /> <br /> &quot;Miss, morning has came ~&quot;, the Maiden shake Wahine's arm gently. She heard one of the warrior mention captain Phi Ho, she should probably think of some responses for the barrage of questions that is about to come from him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T17:59:52-07:00","id":453467,"title":"","content":"&quot;I'd be happy to come along,&quot; said Pakari as he set down his spoon. And he was, although he was not sure he could explain why. Consciously, he understood that he could be heading into terrible danger, and he did not feel at all ready to face down any kind of demon. Despite that, it felt good to be doing something - anything - to help. Yesterday, things had spun entirely out of his control, and today he had an opportunity to put things back in order. He would deal with threats as they came to him.<br /> <br /> &quot;What's this flying beast?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T00:34:01-07:00","id":455513,"title":"","content":"As the night wore on, the confines of the grotto became a little claustrophobic. Even without the presence of the fair folk, she doubted she would have slept too terribly well. She much preferred a hammock stretched between the upper branches of a tree lazily watching the forest below as cool breezes carried all the scents of the island her way. Someplace where she could both admire the heavens and watch her hunting traps or the comings and goings of unassuming people below. It was amazing how infrequently people thought to look 'up' as they hacked noisily through the forest. Gatherings in the most basic sense where almost always sources of discomfort and awkwardness. The fair folk only worsened what was already an uncomfortable situation.<br /> <br /> As she watched the fair folk in the quiet of the night, she could tell that he was examining people's injuries with great care. Whatever his ultimate motives, he seemed genuinely committed to the role of healer and helper. Her heart pounded when he caught her eye following him curiously with a hint of trepidation, turning into a flutter when he knelt beside her to whisper honeyed words that stung deep. She didn't know what to make of his words. Was be trying to be reassuring and comforting in his own odd way or was he trying to pluck at her emotions for his own amusement? Either way, it did hurt her feelings a little that yet another being saw her only as something damaged, incomplete, or lacking. But he at least could objectively see the spiritual scars as clearly as if it where a scar upon her skin. The only solace perhaps was that the fair folk, in an odd bit or irony, was <i>honest</i> about what he saw in her and and what he thought of it. It was more than she could say about most of the people she'd encountered over the years. People rarely took the time to pierce an enigma and almost always filled the silence with their own narratives. The suitors who'd attempted to court her over the years where the worst of all, enamored not with her but the idea they had created of her and attempted to impose upon her. No suitor had ever taken the time to get to know her and none had taken the time to learn the meaning of her signs. It was clear to her that none of them had any desire to communicate more naturally. It would ruin their illusion.<br /> <br /> With a sigh she lay on her back and let her mind wander, thinking of the gods and spirits that inspired her art, of conceptual designs and how she might make them real, of the magnificent foreign ship tempting her just beyond the shore, of all the beautiful goods she could present to entice their willing support, and of all the fine goods they would surely commission once the crisis was over. As she drifted off to sleep, she even managed a smile as she thought of Sarika the Colored One, her muse to whom she always prayed for inspiration and success in her artistic endeavors. It was to her that she often dedicated her most beautiful works. Turning away from the distraction of the world to pour her heart and soul into something beautiful was at times an act of worship in itself. Comforted by the watchful eye of the Whispering Valley tribesmen, she drifted into dreams of treasure found and forged, of magnificent ships and savage seas, of journeys to exotic lands and bartering across the mysterious East.<br /> <br /> She felt a warm hand on her arm as she drifted at the edge of sleep and wake. Reflexively she reached up with a gentle smile, hands as calloused as a hardened sailor taking the maiden's hand as delicately as if she where a flower on the verge of shedding its petals. As wakefulness came to her, she didn't startle. Instead she simply smiled a friendly, wordless 'good morning' as she tightened her grip and pulled herself into a sitting position. Her wounds where healing far faster than she ever thought possible. Despite her misgivings, she wasn't ungrateful for the fair folk's assistance and she gave the creature a nod of acknowledgement as she retrieved her breakfast. Expressing her gratitude further would be redundant. He could surely taste it in the air. For Kiri, she gave a polite bow of her head and signed words of appreciation as she sat with her breakfast and waited for the rest of the day to unfold. She liked Kiri. The woman had spunk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","user":"Foxsimile","date":". 03-24-2015, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}